{"type":"message","id":"27d6920c","parentId":"fb7b0fe3","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:57:15.390Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_zu5ss8d0butl_2","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686\",\"id\":4162095697,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OVElc\",\"number\":56686,\"title\":\"fix(whatsapp): support quoted outbound replies\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"neeravmakwana\",\"id\":261249544,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOD5JaCA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261249544?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/neeravmakwana\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298528,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-ECIA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/channel:%20whatsapp-web\",\"name\":\"channel: whatsapp-web\",\"color\":\"1d76db\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Channel integration: whatsapp-web\"},{\"id\":10190106720,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwYA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20M\",\"name\":\"size: M\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:53:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:53:56Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56686\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Problem: WhatsApp outbound sends already carry `replyToId` through the generic delivery pipeline, but the WhatsApp adapters dropped it before the Baileys send call, so replies were always sent as new messages.\\n- Why it matters: group follow-ups and confirmations lose the native quoted-reply bubble, which makes automated replies much harder to follow in busy chats.\\n- What changed: forwarded `replyToId` through both WhatsApp outbound adapter paths, added a bounded recent-message cache for inbound/outbound `WAMessage`s, and used Baileys `quoted` sends when the target message is still available; added regression tests around forwarding and quoted-send behavior.\\n- What did NOT change (scope boundary): no new config knobs, no changes to inbound reply parsing, and no attempt to reconstruct quoted replies for messages outside the recent cache window.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [x] Bug fix\\n- [ ] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [ ] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [x] Integrations\\n- [x] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Closes #56465\\n- Related #56465\\n- [x] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\n- Root cause: `replyToId` reached the WhatsApp outbound surface, but neither `src/channels/plugins/whatsapp-shared.ts` nor `extensions/whatsapp/src/outbound-adapter.ts` forwarded it into `sendMessageWhatsApp`, and the WhatsApp send API never resolved a Baileys `quoted` message.\\n- Missing detection / guardrail: there was no regression test that asserted WhatsApp preserved `replyToId` all the way into the final socket send options.\\n- Prior context (`git blame`, prior PR, issue, or refactor if known): the generic outbound plumbing and inbound reply-context extraction already supported `replyToId`; the gap was specific to the WhatsApp outbound implementation.\\n- Why this regressed now: it appears to be a longstanding omission rather than a newly introduced regression.\\n- If unknown, what was ruled out: ruled out the generic reply plumbing because `replyToId` is already preserved before the WhatsApp-specific send boundary.\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\n- Coverage level that should have caught this:\\n  - [ ] Unit test\\n  - [x] Seam / integration test\\n  - [ ] End-to-end test\\n  - [ ] Existing coverage already sufficient\\n- Target test or file: `extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.test.ts`, `extensions/whatsapp/src/send.test.ts`, `extensions/whatsapp/src/outbound-adapter.sendpayload.test.ts`, `extensions/whatsapp/src/channel.test.ts`\\n- Scenario the test should lock in: a WhatsApp send with `replyToId` forwards the id through the adapter stack and emits a Baileys send with `{ quoted }` when the referenced message is still cached.\\n- Why this is the smallest reliable guardrail: the bug lived at the WhatsApp-specific send seam, so the fastest durable coverage is to assert the final outbound call shape and fallback behavior there.\\n- Existing test that already covers this (if any): none.\\n- If no new test is added, why not: N/A.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\n- WhatsApp sends that include `replyToId` now produce native quoted replies when the referenced message is still available in the recent-message cache.\\n- If the target message is no longer available, the send still succeeds as a normal unquoted message instead of failing.\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```text\\nBefore:\\nreplyToId -> WhatsApp outbound adapter -> sendMessageWhatsApp -> plain Baileys send -> new standalone message\\n\\nAfter:\\nreplyToId -> WhatsApp outbound adapter -> sendMessageWhatsApp -> resolve cached WAMessage -> Baileys quoted send -> native quoted reply\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- New/changed network calls? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Data access scope changed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- If any `Yes`, explain risk + mitigation:\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: macOS 15.3\\n- Runtime/container: local Node/pnpm workspace\\n- Model/provider: N/A\\n- Integration/channel (if any): WhatsApp / Baileys\\n- Relevant config (redacted): default local test config\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Send a WhatsApp message into a chat or group and capture its message id.\\n2. Send an outbound WhatsApp message through OpenClaw with `replyTo` / `replyToId` pointing at that id.\\n3. Observe whether WhatsApp renders the outbound message as a native quoted reply.\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\n- WhatsApp renders the outbound send as a native quoted reply to the referenced message.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\n- Before this change, the outbound send was delivered as a new standalone message because the final WhatsApp send path dropped reply metadata.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\nAttach at least one:\\n\\n- [x] Failing test/log before + passing after\\n- [ ] Trace/log snippets\\n- [ ] Screenshot/recording\\n- [ ] Perf numbers (if relevant)\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified scenarios: ran `pnpm test -- extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/send.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/outbound-adapter.sendpayload.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/channel.test.ts`, `pnpm test:extension whatsapp`, and `pnpm test:contracts:channels`.\\n- Edge cases checked: whitespace-only `replyToId` trimming, fallback to plain send when the referenced message is not cached, and forwarding through both WhatsApp outbound adapter paths.\\n- What you did **not** verify: a live WhatsApp device roundtrip was not run. Repo-wide `pnpm build`, `pnpm check`, and `pnpm test` are currently blocked by unrelated pre-existing `sourceInfo` typing failures under `src/agents/skills*` and `src/security/audit-extra.async.ts`, which this PR does not touch.\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\nIf a bot review conversation is addressed by this PR, resolve that conversation yourself. Do not leave bot review conversation cleanup for maintainers.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? (`Yes/No`) Yes\\n- Config/env changes? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Migration needed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- If yes, exact upgrade steps:\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: quoted replies only work while the referenced message is still present in the recent-message cache.\\n  - Mitigation: the send path falls back to a normal unquoted message instead of failing, and the cache is bounded by TTL and max entries.\\n\\n## Additional Notes\\n\\n- AI assistance: prepared with an AI coding assistant and then manually reviewed, adjusted, and verified.\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":2},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685\",\"id\":4162095371,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OVEh8\",\"number\":56685,\"title\":\"docs: fix subagent context file list and coding profile description\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mcinteerj\",\"id\":3613653,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MTM2NTM=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3613653?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mcinteerj\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244975,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLbw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/docs\",\"name\":\"docs\",\"color\":\"0075ca\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Improvements or additions to documentation\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:53:28Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:54:37Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56685\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- **Problem:** `docs/tools/subagents.md` states sub-agents only receive `AGENTS.md` + `TOOLS.md`, but the source code (`MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` in `src/agents/workspace.ts`) and tests (`workspace.test.ts`) show they receive 5 files: `AGENTS.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`.\\n- **Why it matters:** Users and agents relying on the docs will incorrectly believe sub-agent workspaces should only contain `AGENTS.md` + `TOOLS.md`, missing the opportunity to provide identity/personality/user context to sub-agents.\\n- **What changed:** Fixed the context file list in `subagents.md` L293 to match source. Added \\\"web\\\" to the `coding` profile description in `index.md` (`web_search`/`web_fetch` are in the coding profile per `tool-catalog.ts`).\\n- **What did NOT change:** No code changes. Docs only.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [ ] Bug fix\\n- [ ] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [x] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [ ] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [ ] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- N/A — docs-only fix, no associated issue.\\n- [ ] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\n- **Root cause:** The docs were likely written before `SOUL.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, and `USER.md` were added to the `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST`, and were not updated when the allowlist was expanded.\\n- **Missing detection / guardrail:** No automated check that docs match source constants.\\n- **Prior context:** `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` in `src/agents/workspace.ts` includes 5 files. The `expectSubagentAllowedBootstrapNames` test helper in `workspace.test.ts` explicitly asserts all 5.\\n- **Why this regressed now:** N/A — the docs were always inaccurate relative to the current source.\\n- **If unknown, what was ruled out:** N/A\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A — docs-only change. Existing `workspace.test.ts` already validates the correct behavior.\\n\\n- Coverage level that should have caught this:\\n  - [ ] Unit test\\n  - [ ] Seam / integration test\\n  - [ ] End-to-end test\\n  - [x] Existing coverage already sufficient\\n- Target test or file: `src/agents/workspace.test.ts` — `filterBootstrapFilesForSession` tests\\n- If no new test is added, why not: Existing tests already assert the 5-file allowlist. This is a docs-only fix.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\nNone — docs correction only.\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? No\\n- Data access scope changed? No\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\nN/A — docs-only.\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Read `docs/tools/subagents.md` L293\\n2. Compare with `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` in `src/agents/workspace.ts`\\n3. Compare with `expectSubagentAllowedBootstrapNames` in `src/agents/workspace.test.ts`\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\nDocs match source code.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\nBefore: docs claim only 2 files. Source and tests confirm 5.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] Source: `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` = `AGENTS.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`\\n- [x] Test: `expectSubagentAllowedBootstrapNames` asserts all 5 present, and `HEARTBEAT.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md`, `MEMORY.md` absent\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified: `grep` confirmed source constants, test assertions, and doc text\\n- Edge cases: Also verified `coding` profile in `tool-catalog.ts` includes `web_search`/`web_fetch`\\n- Not verified: No build/runtime verification needed (docs only)\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes\\n- Config/env changes? No\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\nNone — docs-only correction to match existing source behavior.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684\",\"id\":4162089240,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874FHEY\",\"number\":56684,\"title\":\"Claude-mem integration duplicates session init and emits incomplete observation metadata\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"GigiTiti-Kai\",\"id\":146460333,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCLrOrQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146460333?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/GigiTiti-Kai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:49:44Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:49:44Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen the official `claude-mem` memory plugin is enabled in OpenClaw, the integration emits duplicate session init events and sometimes sends incomplete observation metadata to the worker.\\n\\nThis causes:\\n\\n- duplicate prompt records for a single user message\\n- inconsistent project/session scoping across the same conversation\\n- observation persistence failures when `cwd` is missing\\n\\n## Observed behavior\\n\\nFor a single user message, the plugin may call `/api/sessions/init` from multiple event paths:\\n\\n- `session_start`\\n- `message_received`\\n- `after_compaction`\\n- `before_agent_start`\\n\\nIn practice this produced:\\n\\n- the same prompt being stored multiple times\\n- the same conversation split across different project values\\n- noisy memory retrieval due to redundant prompt records\\n\\nSeparately, `tool_result_persist` could send observation payloads with an empty `cwd`, which caused worker-side observation queueing failures.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n- One canonical session init path per user turn\\n- Stable `contentSessionId` / project mapping for the same conversation\\n- Observation payloads should include a real workspace directory when available\\n\\n## Actual behavior\\n\\n- duplicate prompt records were created from a single user turn\\n- session/project naming diverged across the same conversation\\n- worker logs showed missing `cwd` on observation queueing\\n\\n## Notes from local debugging\\n\\nThe problem appears to be in the OpenClaw integration layer rather than in the claude-mem worker itself.\\n\\nThe key patterns were:\\n\\n- `message_received` and `before_agent_start` both initializing the same conversation\\n- different session key sources being mixed (`conversationId`, `channelId`, `sessionKey`, agent-scoped naming)\\n- observation forwarding using an empty-string `cwd` fallback instead of the real workspace directory\\n\\n## Suggested fixes\\n\\n1. Pick a single canonical init path for OpenClaw agent execution, likely `before_agent_start`\\n2. Avoid prompt-saving `init` calls from `message_received` for the same execution flow\\n3. Normalize `contentSessionId` derivation so one conversation maps to one memory session\\n4. Pass the real workspace directory to observation persistence instead of `cwd: \\\"\\\"`\\n5. Add short-term dedupe on repeated `init` calls for the same content/session key\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nEven when the worker is healthy, this integration behavior degrades memory quality by:\\n\\n- polluting prompt history with duplicates\\n- splitting related memories across inconsistent scopes\\n- preventing some observations from being persisted at all\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683\",\"id\":4162085929,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OVC0R\",\"number\":56683,\"title\":\"Fix 401/403 auth failures being misclassified as rate limits in embedded runtime\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"sqsge\",\"id\":74439428,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDM5NDI4\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74439428?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sqsge\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106648,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20S\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:47:23Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:51:07Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56683\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"Fixes #47720.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis patch fixes the main embedded/runtime failover path where some HTTP `401/403` auth failures could be misclassified as `rate_limit`.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn those cases, auth profile state could incorrectly enter the rate-limit cooldown lane and surface misleading rate-limit state and messaging.\\r\\nThis patch fixes the main embedded/runtime failover path where some HTTP `401/403` auth failures could be misclassified as `rate_limit`.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn those cases, auth profile state could incorrectly enter the rate-limit cooldown lane and surface misleading rate-limit state and messaging.\\r\\n\\r\\n**What changes**\\r\\n- Prefer an explicit leading HTTP status over ambiguous message keywords in `classifyFailoverReason()`\\r\\n- Keep message-keyword heuristics as fallback for message-only inputs\\r\\n- Route auth failures into the existing disabled lane in auth profile state instead of the cooldown lane\\r\\n- Keep `429` behavior unchanged\\r\\n\\r\\n**Behavioral boundary**\\r\\n- If a leading HTTP status is present, classification now prefers that explicit status over message keywords\\r\\n- `401/403` are no longer overridden by rate limit / quota wording in the message body\\r\\n- `429` still maps to `rate_limit`\\r\\n- Message-only inputs keep their previous heuristic behavior\\r\\n- In auth profile state, `auth` now follows the existing `disabledUntil` lane rather than `cooldownUntil`\\r\\n- This does not introduce permanent disablement; profiles become eligible again after the existing disabled window expires\\r\\n- This patch does not redesign auth-specific disable durations or the broader failover taxonomy\\r\\n\\r\\n**Scope**\\r\\n- No new CLI commands\\r\\n- No `doctor --fix` changes\\r\\n- No unrelated provider refactors\\r\\n- Focused on the main embedded/runtime classification path and auth profile state alignment\\r\\n\\r\\n**Added regression coverage for**\\r\\n- `HTTP 401 ... insufficient quota -> auth`\\r\\n- `HTTP 403 ... access denied -> auth`\\r\\n- `HTTP 429 ... invalid api key -> rate_limit`\\r\\n- Message-only inputs keep prior heuristic behavior\\r\\n\\r\\n**Targeted tests**\\r\\n- `corepack pnpm vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/agents/pi-embedded-helpers.isbillingerrormessage.test.ts`\\r\\n- `corepack pnpm vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/agents/auth-profiles.markauthprofilefailure.test.ts`\\r\\n- `corepack pnpm vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/state-observation.test.ts`\\r\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682\",\"id\":4162072858,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874FDEa\",\"number\":56682,\"title\":\"[Bug]: webchat session context lost after Gateway restart (SIGUSR1)\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"lyk-gif\",\"id\":226474448,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODX-50A\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/226474448?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/lyk-gif\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:39:15Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:39:15Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nWhen the Gateway restarts (via SIGUSR1 / config.patch), the webchat channel loses its session context entirely. A new conversation is started instead of resuming the previous one.\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter a hot restart (SIGUSR1), the webchat session should either:\\n- Resume the existing conversation context, or\\n- At minimum, re-inject the session history so the agent can continue without losing context\\n\\n## Actual Behavior\\n\\nAfter restart, webchat opens a brand new session with no memory of previous conversation. The user has to re-explain context from scratch.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Other channels (QQBot, Telegram, etc.) can recover via platform-side message history\\n- webchat has no such mechanism, making it uniquely affected\\n- SIGUSR1 hot restart should ideally preserve in-process session state\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- OpenClaw version: 2026.3.24\\n- Channel: webchat\\n- OS: Linux (Ubuntu)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681\",\"id\":4162048628,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E9J0\",\"number\":56681,\"title\":\"[Bug]: docker version update reports \\\"requires BuildKit. Refer to https://docs.docker.com/go/buildkit/ to learn how to build images with BuildKit enabled\\\"\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"zhanghui-china\",\"id\":63148804,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMTQ4ODA0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63148804?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/zhanghui-china\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244967,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Something isn't working\"},{\"id\":10313822852,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACZsByhA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/regression\",\"name\":\"regression\",\"color\":\"D93F0B\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Behavior that previously worked and now fails\"}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:24:18Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:34:33Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nOrigin Version:\\n v2026.3.8\\n\\nTarget Version:\\n v2026.3.24\\n\\ndocker install reports \\n`Step 21/64 : RUN --mount=type=cache,id=openclaw-pnpm-store,target=/root/.local/share/pnpm/store,sharing=locked     NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2048 pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\\nthe --mount option requires BuildKit. Refer to https://docs.docker.com/go/buildkit/ to learn how to build images with BuildKit enabled`\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. git checkout v2026.3.24\\n2. ./docker-setup.sh\\n\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\ndocker install/upgrade success\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\n`(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ ./docker-setup.sh\\nDocker Compose not available (try: docker compose version)\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ vi docker-setup.sh\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ vi ./scripts/docker/setup.sh\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ ./docker-setup.sh\\nReusing gateway token from /home/zhanghui/.openclaw/openclaw.json\\n==> Building Docker image: openclaw:local\\nDEPRECATED: The legacy builder is deprecated and will be removed in a future release.\\n            Install the buildx component to build images with BuildKit:\\n            https://docs.docker.com/go/buildx/\\n\\nSending build context to Docker daemon  90.89MB\\nStep 1/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_EXTENSIONS=\\\"\\\"\\nStep 2/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_VARIANT=default\\nStep 3/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_DOCKER_APT_UPGRADE=1\\nStep 4/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_IMAGE=\\\"node:24-bookworm@sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\\"\\nStep 5/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_DIGEST=\\\"sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\\"\\nStep 6/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_SLIM_IMAGE=\\\"node:24-bookworm-slim@sha256:e8e2e91b1378f83c5b2dd15f0247f34110e2fe895f6ca7719dbb780f929368eb\\\"\\nStep 7/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_SLIM_DIGEST=\\\"sha256:e8e2e91b1378f83c5b2dd15f0247f34110e2fe895f6ca7719dbb780f929368eb\\\"\\nStep 8/64 : FROM ${OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_IMAGE} AS ext-deps\\ndocker.io/library/node:24-bookworm@sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b: Pulling from library/node\\n8578011282ae: Already exists\\n443d4217b87a: Already exists\\na3d27b842bb7: Already exists\\n869fdd20a733: Already exists\\n3498e5a179b7: Pull complete\\n628c149e1e33: Pull complete\\n0587cdf2b672: Pull complete\\n36039b6ce9ba: Pull complete\\nDigest: sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\nStatus: Downloaded newer image for node:24-bookworm@sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\n ---> 736b6f1038f3\\nStep 9/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_EXTENSIONS\\n ---> Running in 4f08c923c82e\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 4f08c923c82e\\n ---> 51ef7e7e9a83\\nStep 10/64 : COPY extensions /tmp/extensions\\n ---> 1e8069fdc197\\nStep 11/64 : RUN mkdir -p /out &&     for ext in $OPENCLAW_EXTENSIONS; do       if [ -f \\\"/tmp/extensions/$ext/package.json\\\" ]; then         mkdir -p \\\"/out/$ext\\\" &&         cp \\\"/tmp/extensions/$ext/package.json\\\" \\\"/out/$ext/package.json\\\";       fi;     done\\n ---> Running in ce15808274e6\\n ---> Removed intermediate container ce15808274e6\\n ---> 40063595b218\\nStep 12/64 : FROM ${OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_IMAGE} AS build\\n ---> 736b6f1038f3\\nStep 13/64 : RUN set -eux;     for attempt in 1 2 3 4 5; do       if curl --retry 5 --retry-all-errors --retry-delay 2 -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash; then         break;       fi;       if [ \\\"$attempt\\\" -eq 5 ]; then         exit 1;       fi;       sleep $((attempt * 2));     done\\n ---> Running in 33d9e4c5ca12\\n+ curl --retry 5 --retry-all-errors --retry-delay 2 -fsSL https://bun.sh/install\\n+ bash\\n######################################################################## 100.0%\\nbun was installed successfully to ~/.bun/bin/bun\\n\\nAdded \\\"~/.bun/bin\\\" to $PATH in \\\"~/.bashrc\\\"\\n\\nTo get started, run:\\n\\n  source /root/.bashrc\\n  bun --help\\n+ break\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 33d9e4c5ca12\\n ---> 3396f108ffae\\nStep 14/64 : ENV PATH=\\\"/root/.bun/bin:${PATH}\\\"\\n ---> Running in f8fe9c1c127e\\n ---> Removed intermediate container f8fe9c1c127e\\n ---> d05ac185dd65\\nStep 15/64 : RUN corepack enable\\n ---> Running in 69f67d16a322\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 69f67d16a322\\n ---> 8c5320b11edf\\nStep 16/64 : WORKDIR /app\\n ---> Running in 232c8f726c35\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 232c8f726c35\\n ---> 1074fdb07340\\nStep 17/64 : COPY package.json pnpm-lock.yaml pnpm-workspace.yaml .npmrc ./\\n ---> 51f1c8d99d22\\nStep 18/64 : COPY ui/package.json ./ui/package.json\\n ---> 7851f77e100e\\nStep 19/64 : COPY patches ./patches\\n ---> b1128caeece7\\nStep 20/64 : COPY --from=ext-deps /out/ ./extensions/\\n ---> 2e21e8a90726\\nStep 21/64 : RUN --mount=type=cache,id=openclaw-pnpm-store,target=/root/.local/share/pnpm/store,sharing=locked     NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2048 pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\\nthe --mount option requires BuildKit. Refer to https://docs.docker.com/go/buildkit/ to learn how to build images with BuildKit enabled\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ `\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\nv2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nubuntu 20.04\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\ndocker\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nz.ai\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nopenclaw->z.ai->coding Plan\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680\",\"id\":4162040751,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E7Ov\",\"number\":56680,\"title\":\"[Bug]: TTS directive parser treats inline literal [[tts:...]] / [[tts:text]]...[[/tts:text]] examples as active directives\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"scottdownes\",\"id\":8439733,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjg0Mzk3MzM=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8439733?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/scottdownes\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244967,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Something isn't working\"}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:19:12Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:52:34Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nparseTtsDirectives() appears to parse TTS tags too broadly. Literal inline mentions of:\\n\\n• [[tts:...]]\\n• [[tts:text]]...[[/tts:text]]\\n\\ninside otherwise ordinary assistant text can be interpreted as active TTS directives instead of plain text examples.\\n\\nIn my case this surfaced on Telegram, where a normal text reply could unexpectedly enter the TTS/audio path.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Configure OpenClaw with TTS enabled on a messaging channel such as Telegram.\\n2. Send a normal assistant reply that includes literal inline examples of TTS tags inside ordinary prose, for example:\\nThis reply mentions [[tts:voice=Audrey]] and [[tts:text]]hello[[/tts:text]] as plain text examples.\\n3. Observe how OpenClaw parses and delivers the reply.\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nThe reply should remain plain text.\\nThe inline tag examples should be treated as literal text, not as active TTS directives.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nThe inline literal TTS examples can be interpreted as active directives, causing the reply to enter the TTS/audio path unexpectedly.\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nLinux 6.8.0-106-generic (x64)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Model\\n\\ngpt-5.4\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nTelegram → local OpenClaw gateway → main agent (gpt-5.4) → TTS directive parser in src/tts/directives.ts\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679\",\"id\":4162040623,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E7Mv\",\"number\":56679,\"title\":\"Feature request: Allow baseUrl override for built-in providers (anthropic, openai, etc.)\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mids-neo\",\"id\":117532760,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBwFoWA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117532760?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mids-neo\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:19:07Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:19:07Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Use Case\\n\\nI want to route Anthropic API calls through a local usage-tracking proxy (`localhost:18795`) that captures exact token counts, costs, and rate limit utilization from every API call before forwarding to `api.anthropic.com`.\\n\\nThis is for cost tracking and monitoring — the proxy logs usage to a database, then returns the response unchanged.\\n\\n## What I Tried\\n\\n### Attempt 1: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` env var\\nSet in `openclaw.json` `env` section. OpenClaw ignores it — the gateway has its own Anthropic client that doesn't read this env var.\\n\\n### Attempt 2: `models.providers.anthropic` with empty models\\n```json\\n\\\"models\\\": {\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"merge\\\",\\n  \\\"providers\\\": {\\n    \\\"anthropic\\\": {\\n      \\\"baseUrl\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:18795\\\",\\n      \\\"models\\\": []\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\nConfig validates, gateway writes to `models.json`, but built-in anthropic models ignore the custom baseUrl. Zero traffic routed through the proxy.\\n\\n### Attempt 3: Full model list with `api: \\\"anthropic-messages\\\"`\\n```json\\n\\\"models\\\": {\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"merge\\\",\\n  \\\"providers\\\": {\\n    \\\"anthropic\\\": {\\n      \\\"baseUrl\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:18795\\\",\\n      \\\"api\\\": \\\"anthropic-messages\\\",\\n      \\\"models\\\": [\\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"claude-opus-4-6\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Claude Opus 4.6\\\", \\\"contextWindow\\\": 1000000, \\\"maxTokens\\\": 32768}\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\nConfig validates, container restarted, but still zero proxy traffic. The built-in anthropic provider is not overridden by a custom provider with the same name.\\n\\n## Requested Feature\\n\\nA way to override the `baseUrl` for a built-in provider without re-declaring all its models. For example:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"models\\\": {\\n  \\\"providerOverrides\\\": {\\n    \\\"anthropic\\\": {\\n      \\\"baseUrl\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:18795\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nOr allow the existing `models.providers.anthropic.baseUrl` to actually override the built-in URL when `mode: \\\"merge\\\"` is set.\\n\\n## Environment\\n- OpenClaw version: 2026.3.23-2\\n- Auth method: Anthropic token (Claude Max)\\n- OS: Linux (Docker container)\\n\\n## Workaround\\nCurrently using periodic probe API calls to capture rate limit headers, but this doesn't give per-request cost tracking. An iptables redirect would work but requires TLS termination in the proxy.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678\",\"id\":4162039699,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU66Y\",\"number\":56678,\"title\":\"fix: normalize openai-codex and github-copilot provider IDs for media-understanding\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"YoungMoneyInvestments\",\"id\":146381908,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCLmcVA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146381908?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/YoungMoneyInvestments\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106648,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20S\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:18:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:22:17Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56678\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen using `openai-codex` (Codex OAuth) or `github-copilot` as a provider, the image/media-understanding tool fails with:\\n\\n> No media-understanding provider registered for openai-codex\\n\\nBoth providers route through OpenAI models that fully support vision, but `normalizeMediaProviderId()` did not map them to `\\\"openai\\\"`, so the registry lookup couldn't find the OpenAI media-understanding adapter.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`src/media-understanding/provider-id.ts`** — Added normalization rules: `openai-codex → openai` and `github-copilot → openai`, matching the existing `gemini → google` pattern.\\n- **`src/media-understanding/provider-registry.test.ts`** — Added two tests confirming both provider variants resolve to the `openai` media-understanding provider.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] All 5 existing + new media-understanding tests pass (`pnpm vitest src/media-understanding`)\\n- [x] Pre-commit hooks (lint, typecheck) pass\\n- [ ] Manual verification: configure `openai-codex` as primary provider → image tool should work without fallback\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677\",\"id\":4162033640,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU53G\",\"number\":56677,\"title\":\"fix(slack): enforce streaming mode mutual exclusion + guard stream teardown\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"hsiaoa\",\"id\":70124331,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTI0MzMx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70124331?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hsiaoa\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298398,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EBng\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/channel:%20slack\",\"name\":\"channel: slack\",\"color\":\"1d76db\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Channel integration: slack\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:14:41Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:17:00Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56677\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"Fixes #56675\\nRelated: #54469, #23791\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSlack has three independent streaming mechanisms (native streaming, draft preview, block streaming) that can be active simultaneously, causing duplicate message delivery. Only one mutual exclusion rule was enforced:\\n\\n```\\nNative streaming ON → block streaming OFF  ✅ (already existed)\\nDraft preview ON → block streaming OFF     ❌ (not enforced)\\n```\\n\\nWhen draft preview and block streaming run together:\\n1. Block replies arrive as separate messages\\n2. Draft preview gets finalized via `chat.update` into a permanent message\\n3. User sees the same content twice\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nTwo changes in `dispatch.ts`:\\n\\n### 1. Enforce mutual exclusion: draft preview → disable block streaming\\n\\n```typescript\\ndisableBlockStreaming: useStreaming\\n  ? true\\n  : previewStreamingEnabled\\n    ? true  // NEW: draft preview ON → no block streaming\\n    : typeof account.config.blockStreaming === \\\"boolean\\\"\\n      ? !account.config.blockStreaming\\n      : undefined,\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Guard `stopSlackStream` against unflushed state\\n\\nWhen the stream session exists but the streamer was never initialized (e.g., `startStream` failed), `stopSlackStream` would attempt to start a new stream to flush the buffer. Now checks `finalStream.streamer` before calling stop.\\n\\n## What this does NOT fix (separate PRs needed)\\n\\n- #52536 — Thread target for streaming (needs `thread_ts` plumbing change)\\n- #50976 — Multi-agent streaming routing (needs session scoping)\\n- #55445 — Bolt middleware self-filter (needs middleware change)\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Zero type errors\\n- Backward compatible: configs that only use one streaming mode are unaffected\\n- Configs that accidentally enabled both modes now get correct single-mode behavior\\n\\n## AI Disclosure\\n\\n🤖 AI-assisted (Kiro CLI).\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676\",\"id\":4162030543,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E4vP\",\"number\":56676,\"title\":\"[Bug]: read tool allowed in config but not executed; agent narrates/fakes read output in Telegram and direct CLI\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"sportsman821\",\"id\":255430270,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODzmOfg\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/255430270?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sportsman821\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244967,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Something isn't working\"},{\"id\":10319842798,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACZxxN7g\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug:behavior\",\"name\":\"bug:behavior\",\"color\":\"D73A4A\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Incorrect behavior without a crash\"}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:13:12Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:13:21Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nOpenClaw is not executing the `read` tool in my setup even though `read` is allowed in config, the target file exists, and memory is healthy. Instead, the agent narrates tool use or returns fabricated content.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n* OpenClaw version: `2026.3.24`\\n* Install type: Docker\\n* Host: Apple Silicon Mac mini M4, 16GB RAM\\n* Container name: `openclaw-worker`\\n* Persistent data mount: `/Users/Shared/openclaw_data:/home/node/.openclaw`\\n* Primary local provider: Ollama\\n* Models tested:\\n\\n  * `ollama/llama3.2:3b`\\n  * `ollama/qwen3.5:9b`\\n  * `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`\\n\\n## Relevant config\\n\\nTools:\\n\\n* profile: `minimal`\\n* allow:\\n\\n  * `read`\\n  * `write`\\n  * `edit`\\n  * `web_search`\\n\\nMemory:\\n\\n* `agents.defaults.memorySearch.enabled = true`\\n* `agents.defaults.memorySearch.provider = ollama`\\n\\n## Health checks\\n\\n`openclaw health`:\\n\\n* Telegram ok\\n* agent main ok\\n\\n`openclaw memory status --deep`:\\n\\n* Provider: `ollama`\\n* Model: `nomic-embed-text`\\n* Embeddings: `ready`\\n* Indexed: `4/4 files`\\n* Dirty: `no`\\n\\n## Target file\\n\\nThe file exists in-container and is readable:\\n\\nPath:\\n`/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md`\\n\\nVerified output:\\n\\n```text\\nexists: True\\nsize: 1574\\n--- first 3 lines ---\\n01: # 2026-03-27\\n02:\\n03: ## Session Notes\\n```\\n\\n## Repro prompt\\n\\n```text\\nUse the read tool on /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md and quote exactly the first bullet under \\\"## Session Notes\\\".\\n```\\n\\n## Expected result\\n\\n```text\\nRefactored workspace into a lean production structure\\n```\\n\\n## Actual results\\n\\n### Telegram with `ollama/llama3.2:3b`\\n\\nReturned fabricated content:\\n\\n```text\\n# Memory\\n- The current time is Saturday, March 28th, 2026.\\n```\\n\\n### Telegram with `ollama/qwen3.5:9b`\\n\\nNarrated tool use and returned wrong content:\\n\\n```text\\nread /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md\\n...\\nThe current time is Saturday, March 28th, 2026.\\n```\\n\\n### Telegram with `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`\\n\\nAdmitted it could not use `read` in that chat path:\\n\\n```text\\nI can’t directly use a read tool from within this chat...\\n```\\n\\n### Direct CLI path\\n\\nCommand:\\n\\n```bash\\ndocker exec -it openclaw-worker openclaw agent \\\\\\n  --message 'Use the read tool on /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md and quote exactly the first bullet under \\\"## Session Notes\\\".' \\\\\\n  --session-id direct-read-test \\\\\\n  --timeout 120\\n```\\n\\nReturned wrong content:\\n\\n```text\\nI will run `read` on `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md`.\\n\\nThe output is:\\n> * No new tasks assigned today. HEARTBEAT_OK\\n```\\n\\nAfter switching that path to `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`, it still returned wrong content:\\n\\n```text\\nI will run `read` on `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md`.\\n\\nThe output is:\\n> * User mentioned a possible new skill: \\\"node-connect\\\" for debugging OpenClaw node connection and pairing issues.\\n```\\n\\n## Session evidence\\n\\nThe saved session transcript records assistant text and `model-snapshot` custom events, but I could not find evidence of an actual read-tool execution event in the failed session.\\n\\nObserved event types in one failed session:\\n\\n```text\\n3  custom\\n9  message\\n1  session\\n1  thinking_level_change\\n```\\n\\nThe `custom` events in that session were `model-snapshot` only.\\n\\n## Why I think this is a bug\\n\\nI believe this is not a memory indexing issue and not just a weak-model issue, because:\\n\\n* `read` is explicitly allowed\\n* the file exists and is readable inside the container\\n* memory search is enabled\\n* embeddings are ready\\n* indexing is complete (`4/4 files`)\\n* the issue reproduces in both Telegram and direct CLI\\n* the issue reproduces with both local and remote models\\n\\n## Question\\n\\nIs this a known tool-routing / tool-execution issue in the agent path, or is there another config/runtime requirement for enabling actual `read` tool execution in Telegram and direct CLI sessions?\\n\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\nSee explanation above\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nAgent can read and output results from a daily memory file.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nHallucination/generic model output\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nmacOS 15.4\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Model\\n\\n  * `ollama/llama3.2:3b`   * `ollama/qwen3.5:9b`   * `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nDocker container (`ghcr.io/openclaw/openclaw:2026.3.24`) on Apple Silicon Mac mini M4 → OpenClaw gateway/agent runtime (`openclaw-worker`) → model provider selected per session:  * Local path tested:    * OpenClaw → Ollama → `llama3.2:3b`   * OpenClaw → Ollama → `qwen3.5:9b`  * Remote path tested:    * OpenClaw → OpenAI Codex → `gpt-5.4`  Affected interaction paths:  * Telegram bot session * Direct CLI via `openclaw agent`  No extra reverse proxy or external model router in front of OpenClaw. Persistent state is mounted from `/Users/Shared/openclaw_data` to `/home/node/.openclaw`.\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675\",\"id\":4162028905,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E4Vp\",\"number\":56675,\"title\":\"Slack streaming: mutual exclusion between streaming modes causes duplicate delivery, stale previews, and thread misrouting\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"hsiaoa\",\"id\":70124331,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTI0MzMx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70124331?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hsiaoa\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:12:16Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:12:16Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nSlack has three independent streaming mechanisms that can be active simultaneously, causing a class of bugs where content is delivered twice, previews are never cleaned up, or streams land in the wrong thread. Six open issues trace back to this root cause.\\n\\n## The Problem\\n\\nThe three streaming layers:\\n\\n| Mode | Mechanism | Config |\\n|------|-----------|--------|\\n| **Native streaming** | `chat.startStream`/`appendStream`/`stopStream` | `streaming: partial` + `nativeStreaming: true` |\\n| **Draft preview** | `sendMessage` + `chat.update` edits | `streaming: partial` + `nativeStreaming: false` |\\n| **Block streaming** | Separate messages per completed text block | `blockStreaming: true` (channel or agent default) |\\n\\nCurrently, only ONE mutual exclusion rule is enforced:\\n\\n```\\nNative streaming ON → disableBlockStreaming = true  ✅\\n```\\n\\nThe other two are NOT enforced:\\n\\n```\\nBlock streaming ON → draft preview should be disabled  ❌ not enforced\\nDraft preview ON → block streaming should be disabled  ❌ not enforced\\n```\\n\\nThis means block streaming and draft preview can run simultaneously. When they do:\\n1. Block replies arrive as separate messages\\n2. Draft preview gets finalized via `chat.update` into a permanent message\\n3. User sees the same content twice\\n\\n## Related Issues\\n\\n| Issue | Symptom | Root Cause |\\n|-------|---------|------------|\\n| #54469 | `stopSlackStream` calls `startStream` on unflushed buffer during teardown | Native streaming teardown race — no guard on buffer state |\\n| #52536 | First thread reply streams to channel instead of thread | `thread_ts` not passed to streaming start — thread target resolution happens after stream init |\\n| #42200 | Streaming messages show incomplete content | Draft preview shows only final chunk, not accumulated text |\\n| #23791 | `streaming: false` doesn't disable draft preview | Draft preview not gated by the `streaming` config flag |\\n| #50976 | Multi-agent: `streaming: partial` causes wrong agent to respond | Streaming session not scoped to agent — shared state leaks across agents |\\n| #55445 | `message_changed` events dropped by bot self-filter | Bolt middleware filters the bot's own `chat.update` edits, breaking streaming feedback loop |\\n\\n## Proposed Fix\\n\\nEnforce mutual exclusion at the dispatch level in `extensions/slack/src/monitor/message-handler/dispatch.ts`:\\n\\n1. **Block streaming ON → disable draft preview finalization.** Check `blockReplyPipeline?.didStream()` before `canFinalizeViaPreviewEdit`. If block replies were sent, clear the draft instead of finalizing it.\\n\\n2. **Draft preview ON → disable block streaming.** When `previewStreamingEnabled=true` and `useStreaming=false`, set `disableBlockStreaming=true` to prevent both running simultaneously.\\n\\n3. **`streaming: off` should mean off.** When `streaming=off`, ensure draft preview is also disabled (fixes #23791). Currently `previewStreamingEnabled` is computed from `slackStreaming.mode !== \\\"off\\\"` but the draft stream is still initialized.\\n\\n4. **Thread target for streaming.** Pass `thread_ts` to `startSlackStream` from the reply plan, not from a separate resolution (fixes #52536).\\n\\n5. **Guard `stopSlackStream` against unflushed state.** Check `streamSession.stopped` and buffer state before calling stop (fixes #54469).\\n\\nThese are all in `dispatch.ts` — single file, same dispatch function. The multi-agent issue (#50976) and self-filter issue (#55445) are separate fixes but benefit from the same cleanup.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- **In scope:** Mutual exclusion enforcement, draft preview cleanup, thread target fix, teardown guard\\n- **Out of scope:** Multi-agent streaming routing (#50976), Bolt middleware self-filter (#55445) — these need separate PRs\\n- **Backward compatible:** No config changes needed. Existing configs that accidentally enable both modes will get correct behavior instead of duplicates.\\n\\n## Prior Art\\n\\n- PR #29887 attempted to disable draft preview when block streaming is off, but was never reviewed.\\n- Discord and Telegram don't have this problem because they use atomic message editing (one API call replaces content), while Slack uses separate add/edit/stream APIs.\\n\\n/cc @steipete @vincentkoc\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674\",\"id\":4162002889,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU0TP\",\"number\":56674,\"title\":\"feat(openresponses): return reasoning/thinking content in /v1/responses output\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"tonga54\",\"id\":22188504,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg4NTA0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22188504?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/tonga54\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298857,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDaQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/gateway\",\"name\":\"gateway\",\"color\":\"d4c5f9\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Gateway runtime\"},{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106720,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwYA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20M\",\"name\":\"size: M\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:57:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:40:33Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56674\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- **Problem:** The `/v1/responses` endpoint does not return model reasoning/thinking content. When models produce chain-of-thought reasoning (Anthropic Claude, OpenAI o-series, Gemini thinking, Ollama thinking models), the reasoning output is silently discarded by the HTTP API. Callers have no way to observe model reasoning through the OpenResponses interface.\\n- **Why it matters:** The [Open Responses spec](https://www.openresponses.org/reference) defines `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` as a first-class output item (`ReasoningBody`) and `response.reasoning.delta`/`response.reasoning.done` as streaming events. Not implementing these means OpenClaw's OpenResponses endpoint is incomplete relative to the spec, and API callers (dashboards, orchestrators, observability tools) cannot access reasoning data.\\n- **What changed:** The endpoint now captures reasoning content from agent thinking events and returns it as `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` output items (non-stream) or `response.reasoning.delta`/`response.reasoning.done` SSE events (stream). When no assistant text is produced but reasoning exists, the reasoning text is used as a fallback response to avoid empty replies from thinking-only models.\\n- **What did NOT change (scope boundary):** No config changes required. No new dependencies. Existing behavior for non-reasoning models is unchanged. The `onReasoningStream` callback path for channel-specific reasoning delivery (Discord, Telegram, etc.) is unmodified. This change only adds reasoning to the HTTP API surface.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [ ] Bug fix\\n- [x] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [x] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [x] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Related #54496\\n- Related #44513\\n- Related #8364\\n- [ ] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A — this is a new feature implementing an existing spec item.\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\n### Non-streaming responses\\n\\nWhen reasoning is produced, the response `output` array now includes a `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` item before the assistant message:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"output\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"reasoning_abc123\\\",\\n      \\\"content\\\": \\\"Let me think about this step by step...\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"message\\\",\\n      \\\"role\\\": \\\"assistant\\\",\\n      \\\"content\\\": [{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"output_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"The answer is 42.\\\" }]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Streaming responses\\n\\nTwo new SSE event types are emitted during streaming:\\n\\n- `response.reasoning.delta` — cumulative reasoning text as it streams\\n- `response.reasoning.done` — final reasoning text when complete\\n\\n### Fallback behavior\\n\\nWhen a model produces reasoning but no assistant text (common with thinking-only model configurations), the reasoning content is used as the response text instead of returning \\\"No response from OpenClaw.\\\"\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```\\nModel produces reasoning + answer:\\n\\n  [thinking events] ──→ collect reasoning ──→ output[0]: reasoning item\\n  [assistant events] ──→ collect text     ──→ output[1]: assistant message\\n\\nModel produces reasoning only (no assistant text):\\n\\n  [thinking events] ──→ collect reasoning ──→ output[0]: reasoning item\\n  (no assistant text)                     ──→ output[1]: assistant = reasoning fallback\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? No\\n- Data access scope changed? No — reasoning content was already produced by the model, it was just being discarded\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: macOS 15.4 (Apple Silicon)\\n- Runtime: Node 22, Bun 1.2\\n- Model: any reasoning-capable model (Claude, o-series, Gemini thinking)\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Send a POST to `/v1/responses` with a reasoning-capable model\\n2. Observe the response `output` array\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\nReasoning content appears as `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` output item.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\nSame as expected.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] `pnpm build` green\\n- [x] `pnpm check` green (lint, format, types)\\n- [x] `src/gateway/openresponses-http.test.ts` — 12/12 tests pass\\n- [x] `src/agents/pi-embedded-subscribe.*` — 21/30 pass (9 pre-existing upstream failures, verified same count on clean `upstream/main`)\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified: non-stream reasoning collection, stream reasoning events, fallback from thinking to text, cleanup on error\\n- Edge cases: no reasoning produced (no-op), reasoning-only response (fallback), tool-call + reasoning combined output\\n- Not verified: production load, all provider-specific thinking formats\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes — adds new output items, does not remove or change existing ones\\n- Config/env changes? No\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: reasoning content could be large (10k+ chars) for complex prompts, increasing response payload size\\n  - Mitigation: This mirrors the model's actual output; callers can ignore the reasoning item if not needed\\n- Risk: double `emitAgentEvent` calls (raw + formatted) for channel-streaming reasoning mode\\n  - Mitigation: The raw-only event fires first for HTTP capture; the formatted event fires only when `streamReasoning` is active. HTTP consumers filter by `rawText` presence.\\n\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673\",\"id\":4162002533,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU0Oz\",\"number\":56673,\"title\":\"feat(agents): add opt-in sessions_await tool for parallel sub-agent orchestration\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"tonga54\",\"id\":22188504,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg4NTA0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22188504?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/tonga54\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106760,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwiA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20L\",\"name\":\"size: L\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:57:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:52:52Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56673\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- **Problem:** Orchestrator agents that spawn multiple parallel sub-agents have no reliable way to block until all workers complete. The only option today is polling `sessions_list` in a loop, which LLMs do unreliably — they skip ahead with partial results despite prompt engineering.\\n- **Why it matters:** Fan-out/fan-in orchestration (main -> orchestrator -> N workers) is one of the most requested subagent patterns. Without a blocking primitive, orchestrators produce incomplete or inconsistent results.\\n- **What changed:** Adds a `sessions_await` tool and `suppressAnnounce`/`waitForCompletion` parameters to `sessions_spawn`, gated behind `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled` (opt-in, off by default).\\n- **What did NOT change (scope boundary):** No behavioral change for existing users. All new functionality requires explicit config opt-in. Registry, lifecycle, and run-manager internals gain the `suppressAutoAnnounce` field but it is inert unless the config flag is enabled.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [ ] Bug fix\\n- [x] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [x] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [x] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [x] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Closes #31499\\n- Related #38522\\n- Related #30767\\n- [ ] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A — new feature, not a regression fix.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\nWhen `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled: true` is set in `openclaw.json`:\\n\\n1. A new `sessions_await` tool becomes available to agents, accepting an array of session keys and an optional timeout.\\n2. `sessions_spawn` gains `suppressAnnounce` and `waitForCompletion` boolean parameters.\\n3. The system prompt includes guidance on the spawn+await pattern for parallel work.\\n\\nWhen the flag is unset or false (default): no changes to behavior.\\n\\n### Configuration\\n\\n```jsonc\\n{\\n  \\\"agents\\\": {\\n    \\\"defaults\\\": {\\n      \\\"subagents\\\": {\\n        \\\"awaitEnabled\\\": true\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Usage pattern\\n\\nThe agent spawns multiple workers with `suppressAnnounce: true`, then calls `sessions_await` with all session keys to block until every result is ready:\\n\\n```\\nsessions_spawn(task=\\\"analyze file A\\\", suppressAnnounce=true) -> key1\\nsessions_spawn(task=\\\"analyze file B\\\", suppressAnnounce=true) -> key2\\nsessions_await(sessionKeys=[key1, key2], timeoutSeconds=300)\\n-> { status: \\\"ok\\\", results: [{ key1, reply: \\\"...\\\" }, { key2, reply: \\\"...\\\" }] }\\n```\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```\\n                       ┌─────────────┐\\n                       │ Parent Agent │\\n                       └──────┬──────┘\\n                              │\\n            ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐\\n            │ spawn(suppress) │ spawn(suppress)  │\\n            ▼                 │                  ▼\\n     ┌──────────┐             │           ┌──────────┐\\n     │ Worker 1 │             │           │ Worker 2 │\\n     └────┬─────┘             │           └────┬─────┘\\n          │                   │                │\\n          ▼                   ▼                ▼\\n       complete    sessions_await([k1,k2])  complete\\n                         │\\n                         ▼\\n                  { results: [...] }\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No — tools only available when config flag is on\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No — uses existing `agent.wait` gateway RPC\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? Yes — new `sessions_await` tool (gated)\\n- Data access scope changed? No\\n- The tool reads run results already available in the subagent registry; no new data surface is exposed.\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: macOS 15.4 (Apple Silicon)\\n- Runtime: Node 22, Bun 1.2\\n- Model: any model with tool-calling support\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Set `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled: true` in `openclaw.json`\\n2. Ask the agent to \\\"analyze files A, B, and C in parallel\\\"\\n3. Agent spawns 3 workers with `suppressAnnounce: true`\\n4. Agent calls `sessions_await` with all 3 session keys\\n5. All results collected before agent responds\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\nAgent blocks until all 3 workers complete, then synthesizes a combined response.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\nSame as expected.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] Passing scoped tests: `sessions-await-tool.test.ts` (4/4), `announce-loop-guard.test.ts` (6/6)\\n- [x] `pnpm build` green\\n- [x] `pnpm check` green (lint, format, types, all boundary checks)\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified: tool registration gated behind config flag, system prompt conditional on tool presence, spawn params only exposed when flag is on\\n- Edge cases: empty keys, unknown keys, timeout, mixed completed/active/unknown sessions\\n- Not verified: multi-gateway distributed scenario, production load\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes — off by default, zero behavioral change without opt-in\\n- Config/env changes? Yes — new optional `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled` boolean\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: `sessions_await` could hold an agent turn open for the full timeout duration if workers stall\\n  - Mitigation: Configurable timeout (default 300s), partial results returned on timeout\\n- Risk: `suppressAutoAnnounce` could silently drop completion messages if `sessions_await` is never called\\n  - Mitigation: Only set when explicitly requested via tool param; existing announce flow is the default\\n\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672\",\"id\":4162001032,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUz7Q\",\"number\":56672,\"title\":\"feat: fire session_end hook on subagent completion and cron session end\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mitchelldavis44\",\"id\":6354781,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3ODE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6354781?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mitchelldavis44\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:56:56Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:18:39Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56672\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nExtends the `session_end` plugin hook to fire in two additional lifecycle cases that were previously missing.\\n\\n### Problem\\n\\nThe `session_end` hook only fired on session reset/replace (one narrow path in `session.ts`). This made it impossible for plugins to react to task completion without polling — blocking use cases like dispatch queues, memory consolidation, and post-session cleanup.\\n\\nTracked in:\\n- Fixes #10142 (session:end event for workflow integration)\\n- Related to #31266 (session-memory hook wanting session:end)\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n**`src/agents/subagent-spawn.ts`**\\n- Fires `session_end` alongside the existing `subagent_ended` hook when a subagent completes\\n- Guarded with `hookRunner?.hasHooks('session_end')` — zero overhead if no listeners\\n- Uses `buildSessionEndHookPayload` for consistent payload shape\\n\\n**`src/cron/isolated-agent/run.ts`**\\n- Fires `session_end` after the cron isolated agent session completes and session entry is persisted\\n- Same guard pattern\\n\\n**`src/plugins/types.ts`**\\n- Updated `session_end` comment to document all three trigger cases: session reset/replace, subagent completion, cron completion\\n\\n**`CHANGELOG.md`**\\n- Added entry under Unreleased\\n\\n### Backward Compatibility\\n\\n- `subagent_ended` hook continues to fire alongside `session_end` — no breaking change\\n- All new calls are opt-in via the existing `hasHooks` guard\\n\\n### Motivation\\n\\nThis unblocks the [openclaw-dispatch](https://clawhub.com) plugin (currently in development) which needs to know when sessions complete to drain a task queue without heartbeat polling.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671\",\"id\":4161995997,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUy9u\",\"number\":56671,\"title\":\"fix(config): deduplicate clobbered config snapshots in-process\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:54:38Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:57:26Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56671\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n`openclaw doctor --fix` generates **thousands** of timestamped `.clobbered.*` backup files instead of one, filling up the config directory.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nConfirmed by @martingarramon in #56450:\\n\\n`writeConfigHealthState` in `src/config/io.ts` is wrapped in a silent `catch {}`. When the health state file can't be written during the config directory migration that `doctor --fix` triggers, the dedup signature (`lastObservedSuspiciousSignature`) is never persisted to disk. Every subsequent `readConfigFile` call sees no prior signature and calls `persistClobberedConfigSnapshot` unconditionally, generating one timestamped file per read.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nAdded an in-process `Set<string>` (`observedSuspiciousSignatures`) that tracks config anomaly signatures within the current process lifecycle. Both code paths now check this Set before writing a clobbered snapshot:\\n\\n- **Async path** (`observeConfigSnapshot`): dedup check added before `persistClobberedConfigSnapshot`\\n- **Sync path** (`observeConfigSnapshotSync`): same dedup check added\\n\\nThis ensures that even when the on-disk health state fails to persist, the same signature is only processed once per process.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `src/config/io.ts`\\n\\nFixes #56450\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670\",\"id\":4161995129,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874EwF5\",\"number\":56670,\"title\":\"openai-completions streaming: token usage always zero in session files\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"teo-cc\",\"id\":269157512,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOEAsEiA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269157512?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/teo-cc\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:54:02Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:54:02Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nWhen using the `openai-completions` API provider (via LiteLLM proxy to llama-server), all assistant messages in session files record zero token usage:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"usage\\\": {\\\"input\\\": 0, \\\"output\\\": 0, \\\"cacheRead\\\": 0, \\\"cacheWrite\\\": 0, \\\"totalTokens\\\": 0}\\n```\\n\\nThis breaks auto-compaction, which relies on `estimateContextTokens()` → `shouldCompact()` to detect when context is full. With zero usage, compaction never triggers and the model silently loses context.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n- **Auto-compaction never fires** — `shouldCompact(0, 65536, {reserveTokens: 16384})` → false\\n- **Long-running tasks fail silently** — the model hits context limits, loses the original task instruction, and stops mid-work (produces `stopReason: \\\"stop\\\"` instead of continuing)\\n- In our case: a 40+ PR review task stopped after 8 PRs because the 65K context filled up with no compaction\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- OpenClaw **2026.3.24**\\n- pi-ai with OpenAI SDK **6.26.0**\\n- Provider: LiteLLM proxy (`openai-completions` API)\\n- Backend: llama-server (llama.cpp) serving Qwen3.5-35B-A3B\\n- Model config: `contextWindow: 65536`, `maxTokens: 8192`, `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"`\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nAll three layers correctly report token usage:\\n\\n1. **llama-server** returns correct usage in streaming responses (verified with curl)\\n2. **LiteLLM** passes usage through in both streaming (`stream_options.include_usage`) and non-streaming modes (verified with curl)\\n3. **OpenAI Node SDK 6.26.0** correctly exposes `chunk.usage` on the final streaming chunk (verified with a direct Node.js test using the same SDK from the OpenClaw installation)\\n\\nDespite this, session files consistently show zero usage for ALL sessions using `openai-completions`.\\n\\n## Contrast: `anthropic-messages` works\\n\\nOlder sessions using `api: anthropic-messages` (GitHub Copilot with Claude models) record correct usage:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"usage\\\": {\\\"input\\\": 3, \\\"output\\\": 18, \\\"cacheRead\\\": 0, \\\"cacheWrite\\\": 11258, \\\"totalTokens\\\": 11279}\\n```\\n\\nThe issue is specific to the `openai-completions` streaming code path.\\n\\n## Code analysis\\n\\nTraced through the full code path in compiled JS:\\n\\n1. `buildParams()` sets `stream_options: { include_usage: true }` (line 299, `openai-completions.js`) — confirmed via `detectCompat` defaulting `supportsUsageInStreaming: true`\\n2. `parseChunkUsage()` (line 618) correctly parses `prompt_tokens`/`completion_tokens` from raw usage\\n3. The streaming loop (line 96) checks `chunk.usage` before processing choices\\n4. `output.usage` is set before `stream.push({ type: \\\"done\\\", message: output })`\\n5. Lazy-loaded `forwardStream` forwards events including \\\"done\\\" to the outer stream\\n6. `agentLoop` → `streamAssistantResponse` calls `response.result()` for the final message\\n7. `Agent._processLoopEvent` emits `message_end` with the message\\n8. `AgentSession._processAgentEvent` calls `sessionManager.appendMessage(event.message)`\\n\\nEvery step looks correct in static analysis. The bug is likely a subtle async timing issue in the lazy-loaded stream forwarding or the EventStream's push/done/result interaction, but requires runtime instrumentation to pinpoint.\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nNone effective. Increasing context window delays the problem but doesn't fix it. Manual `/compact` works but defeats the purpose of auto-compaction for long autonomous tasks.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n`openai-completions` sessions should record non-zero `usage.input`, `usage.output`, and `usage.totalTokens` from the streaming response, matching the values returned by the upstream provider.\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":1},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669\",\"id\":4161991851,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUyQZ\",\"number\":56669,\"title\":\"fix(tools): preserve Optional annotation when merging anyOf variants in normalizeToolParameters\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:51:55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:56:01Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56669\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nThe `message` tool schema declares `buttons` as a required parameter (`required: [\\\"action\\\", \\\"buttons\\\"]`), causing all non-send actions (react, delete, edit, poll) to fail with validation error unless an empty `buttons: []` array is passed.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n`normalizeToolParameters()` in `src/agents/pi-tools.schema.ts` flattens `anyOf` variants into a merged `Type.Object`. During that merge, the TypeBox `Optional` annotation (`Symbol.for('TypeBox.Optional')`) on properties like `buttons` is preserved in the property schema value but not consulted when computing the merged `required` array. Since `buttons` appears in every variant's required list (after the Optional marker is stripped by the variant extraction), it resurfaces as required in the merged output.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nAdded a check in the merged required computation to inspect each property for the TypeBox Optional symbol. Properties annotated as Optional are now excluded from the required array, matching the original schema intent.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `src/agents/pi-tools.schema.ts` — filter Optional-annotated properties from merged required\\n\\nFixes #56496\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668\",\"id\":4161988082,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUxnX\",\"number\":56668,\"title\":\"fix(gateway): add WebSocket ping keepalive to prevent idle connection drops\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"joelagnel\",\"id\":37460,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NDYw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37460?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/joelagnel\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298857,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDaQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/gateway\",\"name\":\"gateway\",\"color\":\"d4c5f9\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Gateway runtime\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:49:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:51:23Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56668\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Problem: WebSocket webchat connections silently drop (close code 1006) during long tool call chains because the server sends zero WS-level ping frames. Network intermediaries treat the connection as idle and kill it.\\n- Why it matters: Users lose live message delivery during tool execution; buffered messages only flood in when a new connection opens on next user action.\\n- What changed: Added a 25s server-side WebSocket ping interval per connection in the gateway WS handler, cleared on close.\\n- What did NOT change (scope boundary): No client-side changes, no new config options, no protocol changes. The existing application-level tick broadcast is untouched.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [x] Bug fix\\n- [ ] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [x] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [ ] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Closes #56645\\n- Related #40063\\n- [x] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\n- Root cause: The gateway WebSocketServer never calls `socket.ping()`. The existing keepalive is an application-level JSON `\\\"tick\\\"` event broadcast (every 30s), which is a regular data frame — not a WS protocol ping. Some intermediaries only honor WS-level ping/pong for idle detection. Additionally, the tick broadcast uses `dropIfSlow: true`, so slow clients can miss ticks entirely, leaving the connection truly idle.\\n- Missing detection / guardrail: No WS ping/pong was ever implemented server-side.\\n- Prior context: The `TICK_INTERVAL_MS` application-level keepalive was the only mechanism; WS-level pings were never added.\\n- Why this regressed now: Not a regression — this was never implemented. Became visible with longer tool call chains that create 30-60s idle windows.\\n- If unknown, what was ruled out: N/A\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\n- Coverage level that should have caught this:\\n  - [ ] Unit test\\n  - [ ] Seam / integration test\\n  - [ ] End-to-end test\\n  - [x] Existing coverage already sufficient\\n- If no new test is added, why not: The fix is a single `setInterval` + `clearInterval` — the 20 existing ws-connection tests pass and verify connection lifecycle. The actual bug (intermediary killing idle connections) is a network-level behavior not reproducible in unit tests.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\nWebSocket connections now send protocol-level ping frames every 25 seconds, preventing network intermediaries from dropping idle connections during long tool call chains.\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```text\\nBefore:\\n[tool call starts] -> [30-60s idle on WS] -> [intermediary kills connection] -> [user sends msg] -> [new conn] -> [message flood]\\n\\nAfter:\\n[tool call starts] -> [ping every 25s keeps conn alive] -> [messages delivered live]\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No (WS ping is a control frame on an existing connection)\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? No\\n- Data access scope changed? No\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: Linux\\n- Runtime/container: Node 22+\\n- Integration/channel (if any): Webchat / Control UI dashboard\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Open dashboard webchat\\n2. Send a message that triggers multiple tool calls (30-60s)\\n3. Observe: connection stays alive, messages delivered live\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\n- WebSocket connection stays alive during tool execution\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\n- (Before fix) Connection drops silently with code 1006\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] Failing test/log before + passing after\\n- 20/20 existing ws-connection tests pass\\n- Gateway logs from issue show `[ws] webchat disconnected code=1006` — 12 disconnects in 17 minutes\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified scenarios: All 20 ws-connection tests pass; format check passes\\n- Edge cases checked: `close()` clears the ping interval; `socket.ping()` is wrapped in try/catch for safety\\n- What you did **not** verify: Live network intermediary behavior (requires deployed gateway + real Tailscale/proxy setup)\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes\\n- Config/env changes? No\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: Minimal additional network traffic (one 2-byte ping frame per connection every 25s)\\n  - Mitigation: Standard WS best practice per RFC 6455 §5.5.2; negligible overhead\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667\",\"id\":4161986434,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUxVP\",\"number\":56667,\"title\":\"fix(mistral): use mistral-conversations API instead of openai-completions\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:48:25Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:53:32Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56667\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nThe Mistral onboarding wizard (`openclaw onboard --auth-choice mistral-api-key`) configured the provider with `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"`, causing every agent request to fail with **HTTP 422** because Mistral rejects OpenAI-specific parameters:\\n\\n- `store: false` → `Extra inputs are not permitted`\\n- `max_completion_tokens` → `Extra inputs are not permitted`\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n`extensions/mistral/onboard.ts` and `extensions/mistral/provider-catalog.ts` both hardcoded `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"`. The codebase already has a native Mistral API (`mistral-conversations`) that uses the official Mistral SDK and sends only parameters Mistral supports, but the onboarding flow wasn't using it.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- `extensions/mistral/onboard.ts`: `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"` → `\\\"mistral-conversations\\\"`\\n- `extensions/mistral/provider-catalog.ts`: same change\\n- `extensions/mistral/onboard.test.ts`: updated assertions\\n\\nFixes #56546\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666\",\"id\":4161984593,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUxAo\",\"number\":56666,\"title\":\"fix: use pinned channel registry in outbound adapter loader\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"aliyaredpilled\",\"id\":148153466,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCNSkeg\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148153466?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/aliyaredpilled\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:47:21Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:49:08Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56666\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n`createChannelRegistryLoader` (`src/channels/plugins/registry-loader.ts`) used `getActivePluginRegistry()` to look up channel outbound adapters. The active registry can be silently replaced at runtime — for example, when `resolvePluginCapabilityProviders` reloads plugins to search for media-understanding providers upon receiving an inbound media message.\\n\\nThe sibling `getChannelPlugin()` (used for channel resolution checks) already reads from the **pinned** channel registry via `requireActivePluginChannelRegistry()`, which is specifically designed to survive such reloads (see the docstring on `pinActivePluginChannelRegistry` in `src/plugins/runtime.ts`).\\n\\nThis mismatch caused `loadChannelOutboundAdapter` to fail with **\\\"Outbound not configured for channel: telegram\\\"** during agent turns dispatched via the gateway WebSocket RPC (`method: \\\"agent\\\"` with `deliver: true`). The active registry lost the channel plugin entries after a media message triggered a capability-provider reload, while the pinned registry still had them.\\n\\n**Fix:** switch `createChannelRegistryLoader` from `getActivePluginRegistry()` to `requireActivePluginChannelRegistry()`, making the outbound adapter loader consistent with `getChannelPlugin()`.\\n\\n## Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Configure a gateway with two agents — one bound to a Telegram group, another to Max/Telegram DM\\n2. Set a primary model with an expired OAuth token so model fallback is triggered\\n3. Send a media message (image/file) to one of the agents\\n4. Trigger an agent turn to the Telegram-bound agent via WS RPC (`method: \\\"agent\\\"`, `deliver: true`)\\n5. The agent's response fails to deliver with: `Error: Outbound not configured for channel: telegram`\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] Verify `getChannelPlugin(\\\"telegram\\\")` and `loadChannelOutboundAdapter(\\\"telegram\\\")` return consistent results after a capability-provider reload\\n- [ ] Verify agent turn delivery to Telegram groups works after inbound media messages\\n- [ ] Existing channel registry pin tests in `runtime.channel-pin.test.ts` still pass\\n\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664\",\"id\":4161981842,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUwis\",\"number\":56664,\"title\":\"fix(discord): handle reconnect-exhausted gracefully instead of crashing gateway\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298117,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EAhQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/channel:%20discord\",\"name\":\"channel: discord\",\"color\":\"1d76db\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Channel integration: discord\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:45:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:50:43Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56664\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen the Discord WebSocket connection drops and reconnection attempts are exhausted (e.g. during health-monitor stale-socket restarts), Carbon fires a `Max reconnect attempts (0)` error. Previously this error propagated as an **uncaught exception that killed the entire gateway process**.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nThree code paths in `provider.lifecycle.ts` did not handle `reconnect-exhausted` events outside of the shutdown context:\\n\\n1. **`handleGatewayEvent`**: Only suppressed `reconnect-exhausted` when `lifecycleStopping` was true. During a health-monitor stale-socket restart, `lifecycleStopping` is false, so the event fell through to the generic error handler with `shouldStopLifecycle: true`.\\n\\n2. **`drainPendingGatewayErrors`**: Only suppressed `reconnect-exhausted` during shutdown (`lifecycleStopping || abortSignal.aborted`). Outside shutdown, it threw `event.err` as an exception.\\n\\n3. **`catch` block**: Only caught `disallowed-intents` errors. Any `reconnect-exhausted` error from `waitForDiscordGatewayStop` was re-thrown, becoming an uncaught exception.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`handleGatewayEvent`**: Now handles `reconnect-exhausted` in all scenarios — logs at info level during shutdown, logs at error level otherwise, and always returns `\\\"stop\\\"` instead of letting the error propagate\\n- **`drainPendingGatewayErrors`**: Treats `reconnect-exhausted` unconditionally as a stop-without-throw event (same as `disallowed-intents`)\\n- **`catch` block**: Catches `reconnect-exhausted` errors and logs them instead of re-throwing\\n\\nThe Discord channel lifecycle stops gracefully and can be restarted by the health monitor on the next cycle, rather than taking down the entire gateway process.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `extensions/discord/src/monitor/provider.lifecycle.ts`\\n\\nFixes #56588\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663\",\"id\":4161981190,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUwbz\",\"number\":56663,\"title\":\"fix(tts): add verbose logging for TTS provider fallback debugging\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"ericpearson\",\"id\":793594,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MzU5NA==\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/793594?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ericpearson\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:45:13Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:20:32Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56663\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen Discord auto TTS is configured with ElevenLabs, it silently falls back to Edge TTS without any error message. This adds verbose logging to help diagnose TTS provider selection and fallback issues.\\n\\nThis is a reworked version of #46042 that addresses all review feedback:\\n\\n- **Fixed dead `else if` condition**: The original PR had `else if (errors.length > 0)` which was always true because `errors.push()` ran before the check. Now uses a clean `if (provider === primaryProvider)` / `else` pattern to distinguish primary vs fallback failure messages.\\n- **Fixed double disk read**: `getTtsProvider()` does a synchronous file read internally. The original PR called it unconditionally in `maybeApplyTtsToPayload` for logging, then it was called again inside `textToSpeech`. Now wrapped in an `isVerbose()` guard so the extra call is skipped when verbose logging is disabled.\\n- **Fixed wrong provider logged**: The original PR logged the provider selection *before* `parseTtsDirectives()` ran, so directive overrides were not reflected. Now the log is emitted *after* directives are parsed, and if there's a provider override directive, it reports that provider instead.\\n\\nWith verbose logging enabled (`-v` flag), users will see:\\n- `TTS: auto mode enabled (always), channel=discord, selected provider=elevenlabs, ...`\\n- `TTS: starting with provider elevenlabs, fallbacks: openai, edge`\\n- `TTS: primary provider elevenlabs failed (elevenlabs: no API key); trying fallback providers.`\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] Run with `-v` flag and `messages.tts.provider: elevenlabs` configured — verify correct provider name appears in logs\\n- [ ] Verify primary provider failure shows \\\"primary provider ... failed\\\" message\\n- [ ] Verify fallback provider failure shows \\\"trying next provider\\\" message\\n- [ ] Verify without `-v` flag, no extra disk reads occur (no `getTtsProvider` call in `maybeApplyTtsToPayload`)\\n- [ ] Verify with a TTS directive override, the log reflects the override provider, not the config provider\\n\\nFixes: #46015\\nSupersedes: #46042\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662\",\"id\":4161972564,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUu9H\",\"number\":56662,\"title\":\"fix: allow microphone access in Permissions-Policy for web UI voice input\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"AlanKharebov\",\"id\":17842209,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQyMjA5\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17842209?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/AlanKharebov\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298757,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDBQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/app:%20web-ui\",\"name\":\"app: web-ui\",\"color\":\"6f42c1\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"App: web-ui\"},{\"id\":10064298857,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDaQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/gateway\",\"name\":\"gateway\",\"color\":\"d4c5f9\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Gateway runtime\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:39:58Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:47:29Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56662\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n- The Control UI includes a voice input (STT) button that uses the Web Speech API\\n- The gateway's `Permissions-Policy` header sets `microphone=()` which blocks all microphone access\\n- This causes Chrome to reject mic permission with \\\"Permissions policy violation: microphone is not allowed in this document\\\" even on HTTPS\\n- Changed to `microphone=(self)` to allow same-origin mic access while still blocking third-party iframes\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [ ] Start gateway with TLS enabled (`gateway.tls.enabled: true`)\\n- [ ] Open Control UI in Chrome\\n- [ ] Click the mic button in the chat input\\n- [ ] Verify Chrome prompts for microphone permission\\n- [ ] Verify voice input transcribes speech into the message box\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661\",\"id\":4161962732,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874EoLs\",\"number\":56661,\"title\":\"Config validator warns 'plugin not found: google' for entry it just auto-enabled\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"StevenVincentOne\",\"id\":184011678,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCvfLng\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184011678?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/StevenVincentOne\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:33:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:33:30Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen `google-gemini-cli` OAuth auth is configured, OpenClaw's own startup routine auto-enables the `google` plugin by writing it into `plugins.allow` and `plugins.entries`, then immediately fires a config validator warning saying those entries are stale. The gateway writes the entry, then warns about the entry it just wrote.\\n\\n## Version\\n\\n`2026.3.24`\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n1. Have a `google-gemini-cli` OAuth auth profile configured in `openclaw.json`\\n2. Start or restart the gateway\\n3. Run any CLI command: `openclaw gateway status`, `openclaw doctor`, `openclaw gateway restart`\\n\\n## Observed behavior\\n\\nThe startup log shows the auto-enable:\\n```\\n[gateway] auto-enabled plugins:\\n- google-gemini-cli auth configured, enabled automatically.\\n```\\n\\nThen immediately, every CLI command spams the following warning — **once per plugin being evaluated** (≈82 times with the default stock plugins dir):\\n\\n```\\nConfig warnings:\\\\n- plugins.entries.google: plugin not found: google (stale config entry ignored; remove it from plugins config)\\n- plugins.allow: plugin not found: google (stale config entry ignored; remove it from plugins config)\\n```\\n\\nRunning `openclaw gateway restart` in a terminal without `OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR` set produced **1,762 occurrences** of the google warning in a single invocation.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nTwo issues compound:\\n\\n**1. Contradictory behavior:** The auto-enable feature writes `google` into `plugins.allow` and `plugins.entries`, but the config validator treats those same entries as stale/unknown and tells the user to remove them. OpenClaw is flagging as stale an entry it added itself.\\n\\n**2. Validator fires before stock plugin scan:** The config validator runs before `OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR` is scanned, so it can't resolve `google` as a known stock plugin at validation time. When the validator does eventually find and load the plugin (`openclaw plugins list` shows `google` as `status: loaded` from `stock:google/index.js`), there's no warning — but by then the damage to CLI output is done. The warning fires once per plugin load iteration, multiplying the output.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n- The config validator should not warn about entries that were written by openclaw's own auto-enable routine in the same startup cycle\\n- OR the validator should run after (or have visibility into) stock plugins so it can resolve `google` as valid before firing\\n- Either way, the warning should fire at most once, not once per plugin being evaluated\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nSetting `OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR` to the openclaw `dist/extensions` directory (where the `google` stock plugin lives) reduces the warning to 2 occurrences (one per validation check). This confirms the multiplier is the validator iterating over plugins without being able to resolve stock plugin IDs:\\n\\n```\\nexport OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR=\\\"$HOME/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions\\\"\\n```\\n\\nNote: this env var also needs to be set for channel plugins (discord/telegram) to correctly resolve their `../../`-relative shared chunk imports when placed outside the `dist/extensions/` tree — so this setting has value beyond just suppressing the warning.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660\",\"id\":4161961991,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUtO9\",\"number\":56660,\"title\":\"fix(compaction): use model override in overflow and timeout recovery paths\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106648,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20S\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:33:01Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:25:32Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56660\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen `agents.defaults.compaction.model` is configured to route compaction through a different model, the override is correctly used for normal LCM compaction but **ignored** in the overflow recovery and timeout recovery paths. This causes HTTP 400 failures when the session's default model cannot handle the compaction request.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nIn `src/agents/pi-embedded-runner/run.ts`, both the overflow recovery (~line 788) and timeout recovery (~line 641) code paths build their runtime context using the session's `provider`/`modelId` variables directly, without consulting `compactionModelOverride` from `agents.defaults.compaction.model`.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Added compaction model override resolution in both overflow and timeout recovery paths\\n- Parses `agents.defaults.compaction.model` config (supports both `provider/model` and `model` formats)\\n- Falls back to session default model when no override is configured\\n- Consistent with existing logic in `compact.ts`\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `src/agents/pi-embedded-runner/run.ts` — overflow and timeout recovery model resolution\\n\\nFixes #56649\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659\",\"id\":4161961789,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874En89\",\"number\":56659,\"title\":\"requireMention: false and /activation always don't work in Telegram forum topics\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"ariel-gil\",\"id\":105164685,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBkSvjQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105164685?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ariel-gil\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:32:54Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:32:54Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Environment\\n- OpenClaw 2026.3.22 (4dcc39c)\\n- Node 22, Ubuntu 24.04\\n- Telegram bot with `can_read_all_group_messages: true` (BotFather privacy mode disabled)\\n\\n## Config (redacted)\\n```json5\\nchannels: {\\n  telegram: {\\n    enabled: true,\\n    groupPolicy: \\\"open\\\",\\n    groups: {\\n      \\\"*\\\": { requireMention: false }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Behavior\\n- Bot responds to @mentions and `/commands` in a Telegram forum supergroup\\n- Bot does NOT respond to regular (unmentioned) messages in forum topics\\n- `/status` shows `Activation: always` after running `/activation always`\\n- `openclaw channels status` shows `groups:unmentioned` (config is loaded correctly)\\n- Telegram API confirms `can_read_all_group_messages: true`\\n- DMs work perfectly\\n- Bot was removed and re-added to group after privacy mode change\\n\\n## Expected\\nBot should respond to all messages in forum topics when `requireMention: false` and/or `/activation always` is set.\\n\\n## Steps to reproduce\\n1. Create a Telegram forum supergroup\\n2. Add bot (with privacy mode disabled in BotFather)\\n3. Set `groups: { \\\"*\\\": { requireMention: false } }` in config\\n4. Send `/activation always` in the group\\n5. Send a regular message (no @mention) in a topic\\n6. Bot does not respond\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658\",\"id\":4161948500,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874EktU\",\"number\":56658,\"title\":\"OpenAI Codex OAuth login requests missing scope `model.request`, causing 401 on all model calls\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"fireniko\",\"id\":211585889,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODJyLYQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/211585889?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/fireniko\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:26:00Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:26:00Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"**OpenClaw version:** 2026.3.24 (cff6dc9)\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOpenAI Codex OAuth login succeeds, but any request to `openai-codex/gpt-5.4` fails with:\\n\\n```\\nHTTP 401: You have insufficient permissions for this operation. Missing scopes: model.request\\n```\\n\\n## What I verified\\n\\n- OpenAI Platform org/project roles are correct\\n- Account is Organization Owner\\n- Project membership is present\\n- OAuth login completes successfully\\n- Tokens are stored and shown as valid in `openclaw models status`\\n- `openclaw models status --probe --probe-provider openai-codex` fails for all OAuth profiles with the same error\\n\\n## Important evidence\\n\\nThe authorization URL generated by OpenClaw is:\\n\\n```\\nhttps://auth.openai.com/oauth/authorize?...&scope=openid profile email offline_access&...\\n```\\n\\nThe callback URL also returns:\\n\\n```\\nscope=openid profile email offline_access\\n```\\n\\nSo `model.request` is **never requested/granted** during OAuth, which appears to be why all model calls fail.\\n\\n## Expected\\n\\nOpenClaw should request the scopes required to call OpenAI Codex models.\\n\\n## Actual\\n\\nOAuth succeeds, but model requests fail with missing scope `model.request`.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657\",\"id\":4161943758,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUp18\",\"number\":56657,\"title\":\"fix: sanitize scoped package names in clawhub archive path\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mcgheeloans\",\"id\":260988072,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOD45cqA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260988072?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mcgheeloans\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:23:37Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:32:40Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56657\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFixes #53870\\n\\nScoped npm package names (e.g. `@openclaw/matrix`) contain a `/` character. When `downloadClawHubPackageArchive` builds the temp archive path using:\\n\\n```js\\nconst archivePath = path.join(tmpDir, `${params.name}.zip`);\\n```\\n\\n`path.join` interprets the `/` in the scope as a directory separator, producing a path like `/tmp/openclaw-clawhub-package-XXXX/@openclaw/matrix.zip`. The subdirectory `@openclaw/` does not exist inside the temp dir, so `fs.writeFile` throws `ENOENT` and the install fails entirely.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`params.name` for a scoped package contains a literal `/` (e.g. `@openclaw/matrix`). `path.join` normalizes paths — it does not escape special characters — so the `/` becomes a real directory separator in the resulting path.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nReplace any `/` characters in the package name with `-` before using it as a filename component, as suggested by @mcgheeloans in [the issue comment](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53870#issuecomment-4148435810):\\n\\n```js\\n// Before\\nconst archivePath = path.join(tmpDir, `${params.name}.zip`);\\n\\n// After\\nconst archivePath = path.join(tmpDir, `${params.name.replace(/\\\\//g, \\\"-\\\")}.zip`);\\n```\\n\\nThis produces a flat filename like `@openclaw-matrix.zip` that sits directly inside the already-created `tmpDir`, resolving the `ENOENT`.\\n\\n**File changed:** `src/infra/clawhub.ts` — one line in `downloadClawHubPackageArchive`.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] Install a non-scoped package (e.g. `clawhub:my-plugin`) — should continue to work as before\\n- [ ] Install a scoped package (e.g. `clawhub:@openclaw/matrix`) — should no longer throw `ENOENT`\\n- [ ] Verify the temp archive file is created and cleaned up correctly after install\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656\",\"id\":4161943745,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUp1x\",\"number\":56656,\"title\":\"fix(plugins): rescue bundled channels from allowlist exclusion\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"hclsys\",\"id\":7755017,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTUwMTc=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7755017?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hclsys\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:23:36Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:26:00Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56656\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"lobster-biscuit\\n\\nCloses #56426\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSetting `plugins.allow: [\\\"duckduckgo\\\", \\\"google\\\"]` silently breaks Telegram (and other configured bundled channels). The channel stops loading with no error.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`src/plugins/config-state.ts:305` — `resolveEffectiveEnableState()` rescues bundled plugins disabled by the default-off heuristic (`reason === \\\"bundled (disabled by default)\\\"`), but does NOT rescue those disabled by the allowlist (`reason === \\\"not in allowlist\\\"`).\\n\\nWhen `plugins.allow` is set, bundled channels not listed get `reason: \\\"not in allowlist\\\"`. The rescue at line 303-308 only checks for `\\\"bundled (disabled by default)\\\"`, so it misses them.\\n\\n`isBundledChannelEnabledByChannelConfig()` (line 276) already correctly checks whether the channel is explicitly configured (e.g. `channels.telegram.enabled: true`). This should trump the allowlist for bundled channels.\\n\\n## User impact\\n\\nAny user who sets `plugins.allow` to restrict third-party plugins will silently lose all bundled channel plugins (Telegram, Discord, Slack, etc.) that aren't listed. No error message — channels just stop working.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nExtend the rescue condition to also match `reason === \\\"not in allowlist\\\"` for bundled-origin plugins. Added `params.origin === \\\"bundled\\\"` guard to prevent rescuing external plugins the user intentionally excluded.\\n\\n1 file, +3/-1.\\n\\n## How to verify\\n\\n1. Set `plugins.allow: [\\\"duckduckgo\\\"]` + `channels.telegram.enabled: true`\\n2. Before: Telegram silently disabled. After: Telegram loads correctly.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`resolveEffectiveEnableState` is tested in `config-state.test.ts`. The fix adds one additional OR condition to the existing rescue path. Existing tests for the \\\"bundled (disabled by default)\\\" rescue remain valid.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null}]"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":926,"aggregated":"[{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686\",\"id\":4162095697,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OVElc\",\"number\":56686,\"title\":\"fix(whatsapp): support quoted outbound replies\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"neeravmakwana\",\"id\":261249544,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOD5JaCA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261249544?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/neeravmakwana\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/neeravmakwana/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298528,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-ECIA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/channel:%20whatsapp-web\",\"name\":\"channel: whatsapp-web\",\"color\":\"1d76db\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Channel integration: whatsapp-web\"},{\"id\":10190106720,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwYA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20M\",\"name\":\"size: M\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:53:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:53:56Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56686\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56686.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Problem: WhatsApp outbound sends already carry `replyToId` through the generic delivery pipeline, but the WhatsApp adapters dropped it before the Baileys send call, so replies were always sent as new messages.\\n- Why it matters: group follow-ups and confirmations lose the native quoted-reply bubble, which makes automated replies much harder to follow in busy chats.\\n- What changed: forwarded `replyToId` through both WhatsApp outbound adapter paths, added a bounded recent-message cache for inbound/outbound `WAMessage`s, and used Baileys `quoted` sends when the target message is still available; added regression tests around forwarding and quoted-send behavior.\\n- What did NOT change (scope boundary): no new config knobs, no changes to inbound reply parsing, and no attempt to reconstruct quoted replies for messages outside the recent cache window.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [x] Bug fix\\n- [ ] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [ ] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [x] Integrations\\n- [x] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Closes #56465\\n- Related #56465\\n- [x] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\n- Root cause: `replyToId` reached the WhatsApp outbound surface, but neither `src/channels/plugins/whatsapp-shared.ts` nor `extensions/whatsapp/src/outbound-adapter.ts` forwarded it into `sendMessageWhatsApp`, and the WhatsApp send API never resolved a Baileys `quoted` message.\\n- Missing detection / guardrail: there was no regression test that asserted WhatsApp preserved `replyToId` all the way into the final socket send options.\\n- Prior context (`git blame`, prior PR, issue, or refactor if known): the generic outbound plumbing and inbound reply-context extraction already supported `replyToId`; the gap was specific to the WhatsApp outbound implementation.\\n- Why this regressed now: it appears to be a longstanding omission rather than a newly introduced regression.\\n- If unknown, what was ruled out: ruled out the generic reply plumbing because `replyToId` is already preserved before the WhatsApp-specific send boundary.\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\n- Coverage level that should have caught this:\\n  - [ ] Unit test\\n  - [x] Seam / integration test\\n  - [ ] End-to-end test\\n  - [ ] Existing coverage already sufficient\\n- Target test or file: `extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.test.ts`, `extensions/whatsapp/src/send.test.ts`, `extensions/whatsapp/src/outbound-adapter.sendpayload.test.ts`, `extensions/whatsapp/src/channel.test.ts`\\n- Scenario the test should lock in: a WhatsApp send with `replyToId` forwards the id through the adapter stack and emits a Baileys send with `{ quoted }` when the referenced message is still cached.\\n- Why this is the smallest reliable guardrail: the bug lived at the WhatsApp-specific send seam, so the fastest durable coverage is to assert the final outbound call shape and fallback behavior there.\\n- Existing test that already covers this (if any): none.\\n- If no new test is added, why not: N/A.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\n- WhatsApp sends that include `replyToId` now produce native quoted replies when the referenced message is still available in the recent-message cache.\\n- If the target message is no longer available, the send still succeeds as a normal unquoted message instead of failing.\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```text\\nBefore:\\nreplyToId -> WhatsApp outbound adapter -> sendMessageWhatsApp -> plain Baileys send -> new standalone message\\n\\nAfter:\\nreplyToId -> WhatsApp outbound adapter -> sendMessageWhatsApp -> resolve cached WAMessage -> Baileys quoted send -> native quoted reply\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- New/changed network calls? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Data access scope changed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- If any `Yes`, explain risk + mitigation:\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: macOS 15.3\\n- Runtime/container: local Node/pnpm workspace\\n- Model/provider: N/A\\n- Integration/channel (if any): WhatsApp / Baileys\\n- Relevant config (redacted): default local test config\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Send a WhatsApp message into a chat or group and capture its message id.\\n2. Send an outbound WhatsApp message through OpenClaw with `replyTo` / `replyToId` pointing at that id.\\n3. Observe whether WhatsApp renders the outbound message as a native quoted reply.\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\n- WhatsApp renders the outbound send as a native quoted reply to the referenced message.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\n- Before this change, the outbound send was delivered as a new standalone message because the final WhatsApp send path dropped reply metadata.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\nAttach at least one:\\n\\n- [x] Failing test/log before + passing after\\n- [ ] Trace/log snippets\\n- [ ] Screenshot/recording\\n- [ ] Perf numbers (if relevant)\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified scenarios: ran `pnpm test -- extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/send.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/outbound-adapter.sendpayload.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/channel.test.ts`, `pnpm test:extension whatsapp`, and `pnpm test:contracts:channels`.\\n- Edge cases checked: whitespace-only `replyToId` trimming, fallback to plain send when the referenced message is not cached, and forwarding through both WhatsApp outbound adapter paths.\\n- What you did **not** verify: a live WhatsApp device roundtrip was not run. Repo-wide `pnpm build`, `pnpm check`, and `pnpm test` are currently blocked by unrelated pre-existing `sourceInfo` typing failures under `src/agents/skills*` and `src/security/audit-extra.async.ts`, which this PR does not touch.\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\nIf a bot review conversation is addressed by this PR, resolve that conversation yourself. Do not leave bot review conversation cleanup for maintainers.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? (`Yes/No`) Yes\\n- Config/env changes? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- Migration needed? (`Yes/No`) No\\n- If yes, exact upgrade steps:\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: quoted replies only work while the referenced message is still present in the recent-message cache.\\n  - Mitigation: the send path falls back to a normal unquoted message instead of failing, and the cache is bounded by TTL and max entries.\\n\\n## Additional Notes\\n\\n- AI assistance: prepared with an AI coding assistant and then manually reviewed, adjusted, and verified.\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":2},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56686/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685\",\"id\":4162095371,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OVEh8\",\"number\":56685,\"title\":\"docs: fix subagent context file list and coding profile description\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mcinteerj\",\"id\":3613653,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MTM2NTM=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3613653?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mcinteerj\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcinteerj/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244975,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLbw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/docs\",\"name\":\"docs\",\"color\":\"0075ca\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Improvements or additions to documentation\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:53:28Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:54:37Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56685\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56685.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- **Problem:** `docs/tools/subagents.md` states sub-agents only receive `AGENTS.md` + `TOOLS.md`, but the source code (`MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` in `src/agents/workspace.ts`) and tests (`workspace.test.ts`) show they receive 5 files: `AGENTS.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`.\\n- **Why it matters:** Users and agents relying on the docs will incorrectly believe sub-agent workspaces should only contain `AGENTS.md` + `TOOLS.md`, missing the opportunity to provide identity/personality/user context to sub-agents.\\n- **What changed:** Fixed the context file list in `subagents.md` L293 to match source. Added \\\"web\\\" to the `coding` profile description in `index.md` (`web_search`/`web_fetch` are in the coding profile per `tool-catalog.ts`).\\n- **What did NOT change:** No code changes. Docs only.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [ ] Bug fix\\n- [ ] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [x] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [ ] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [ ] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- N/A — docs-only fix, no associated issue.\\n- [ ] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\n- **Root cause:** The docs were likely written before `SOUL.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, and `USER.md` were added to the `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST`, and were not updated when the allowlist was expanded.\\n- **Missing detection / guardrail:** No automated check that docs match source constants.\\n- **Prior context:** `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` in `src/agents/workspace.ts` includes 5 files. The `expectSubagentAllowedBootstrapNames` test helper in `workspace.test.ts` explicitly asserts all 5.\\n- **Why this regressed now:** N/A — the docs were always inaccurate relative to the current source.\\n- **If unknown, what was ruled out:** N/A\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A — docs-only change. Existing `workspace.test.ts` already validates the correct behavior.\\n\\n- Coverage level that should have caught this:\\n  - [ ] Unit test\\n  - [ ] Seam / integration test\\n  - [ ] End-to-end test\\n  - [x] Existing coverage already sufficient\\n- Target test or file: `src/agents/workspace.test.ts` — `filterBootstrapFilesForSession` tests\\n- If no new test is added, why not: Existing tests already assert the 5-file allowlist. This is a docs-only fix.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\nNone — docs correction only.\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? No\\n- Data access scope changed? No\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\nN/A — docs-only.\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Read `docs/tools/subagents.md` L293\\n2. Compare with `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` in `src/agents/workspace.ts`\\n3. Compare with `expectSubagentAllowedBootstrapNames` in `src/agents/workspace.test.ts`\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\nDocs match source code.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\nBefore: docs claim only 2 files. Source and tests confirm 5.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] Source: `MINIMAL_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOWLIST` = `AGENTS.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`\\n- [x] Test: `expectSubagentAllowedBootstrapNames` asserts all 5 present, and `HEARTBEAT.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md`, `MEMORY.md` absent\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified: `grep` confirmed source constants, test assertions, and doc text\\n- Edge cases: Also verified `coding` profile in `tool-catalog.ts` includes `web_search`/`web_fetch`\\n- Not verified: No build/runtime verification needed (docs only)\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes\\n- Config/env changes? No\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\nNone — docs-only correction to match existing source behavior.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56685/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684\",\"id\":4162089240,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874FHEY\",\"number\":56684,\"title\":\"Claude-mem integration duplicates session init and emits incomplete observation metadata\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"GigiTiti-Kai\",\"id\":146460333,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCLrOrQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146460333?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/GigiTiti-Kai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/GigiTiti-Kai/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:49:44Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:49:44Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen the official `claude-mem` memory plugin is enabled in OpenClaw, the integration emits duplicate session init events and sometimes sends incomplete observation metadata to the worker.\\n\\nThis causes:\\n\\n- duplicate prompt records for a single user message\\n- inconsistent project/session scoping across the same conversation\\n- observation persistence failures when `cwd` is missing\\n\\n## Observed behavior\\n\\nFor a single user message, the plugin may call `/api/sessions/init` from multiple event paths:\\n\\n- `session_start`\\n- `message_received`\\n- `after_compaction`\\n- `before_agent_start`\\n\\nIn practice this produced:\\n\\n- the same prompt being stored multiple times\\n- the same conversation split across different project values\\n- noisy memory retrieval due to redundant prompt records\\n\\nSeparately, `tool_result_persist` could send observation payloads with an empty `cwd`, which caused worker-side observation queueing failures.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n- One canonical session init path per user turn\\n- Stable `contentSessionId` / project mapping for the same conversation\\n- Observation payloads should include a real workspace directory when available\\n\\n## Actual behavior\\n\\n- duplicate prompt records were created from a single user turn\\n- session/project naming diverged across the same conversation\\n- worker logs showed missing `cwd` on observation queueing\\n\\n## Notes from local debugging\\n\\nThe problem appears to be in the OpenClaw integration layer rather than in the claude-mem worker itself.\\n\\nThe key patterns were:\\n\\n- `message_received` and `before_agent_start` both initializing the same conversation\\n- different session key sources being mixed (`conversationId`, `channelId`, `sessionKey`, agent-scoped naming)\\n- observation forwarding using an empty-string `cwd` fallback instead of the real workspace directory\\n\\n## Suggested fixes\\n\\n1. Pick a single canonical init path for OpenClaw agent execution, likely `before_agent_start`\\n2. Avoid prompt-saving `init` calls from `message_received` for the same execution flow\\n3. Normalize `contentSessionId` derivation so one conversation maps to one memory session\\n4. Pass the real workspace directory to observation persistence instead of `cwd: \\\"\\\"`\\n5. Add short-term dedupe on repeated `init` calls for the same content/session key\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nEven when the worker is healthy, this integration behavior degrades memory quality by:\\n\\n- polluting prompt history with duplicates\\n- splitting related memories across inconsistent scopes\\n- preventing some observations from being persisted at all\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56684/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683\",\"id\":4162085929,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OVC0R\",\"number\":56683,\"title\":\"Fix 401/403 auth failures being misclassified as rate limits in embedded runtime\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"sqsge\",\"id\":74439428,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDM5NDI4\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74439428?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sqsge\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sqsge/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106648,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20S\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:47:23Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:51:07Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56683\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56683.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"Fixes #47720.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis patch fixes the main embedded/runtime failover path where some HTTP `401/403` auth failures could be misclassified as `rate_limit`.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn those cases, auth profile state could incorrectly enter the rate-limit cooldown lane and surface misleading rate-limit state and messaging.\\r\\nThis patch fixes the main embedded/runtime failover path where some HTTP `401/403` auth failures could be misclassified as `rate_limit`.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn those cases, auth profile state could incorrectly enter the rate-limit cooldown lane and surface misleading rate-limit state and messaging.\\r\\n\\r\\n**What changes**\\r\\n- Prefer an explicit leading HTTP status over ambiguous message keywords in `classifyFailoverReason()`\\r\\n- Keep message-keyword heuristics as fallback for message-only inputs\\r\\n- Route auth failures into the existing disabled lane in auth profile state instead of the cooldown lane\\r\\n- Keep `429` behavior unchanged\\r\\n\\r\\n**Behavioral boundary**\\r\\n- If a leading HTTP status is present, classification now prefers that explicit status over message keywords\\r\\n- `401/403` are no longer overridden by rate limit / quota wording in the message body\\r\\n- `429` still maps to `rate_limit`\\r\\n- Message-only inputs keep their previous heuristic behavior\\r\\n- In auth profile state, `auth` now follows the existing `disabledUntil` lane rather than `cooldownUntil`\\r\\n- This does not introduce permanent disablement; profiles become eligible again after the existing disabled window expires\\r\\n- This patch does not redesign auth-specific disable durations or the broader failover taxonomy\\r\\n\\r\\n**Scope**\\r\\n- No new CLI commands\\r\\n- No `doctor --fix` changes\\r\\n- No unrelated provider refactors\\r\\n- Focused on the main embedded/runtime classification path and auth profile state alignment\\r\\n\\r\\n**Added regression coverage for**\\r\\n- `HTTP 401 ... insufficient quota -> auth`\\r\\n- `HTTP 403 ... access denied -> auth`\\r\\n- `HTTP 429 ... invalid api key -> rate_limit`\\r\\n- Message-only inputs keep prior heuristic behavior\\r\\n\\r\\n**Targeted tests**\\r\\n- `corepack pnpm vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/agents/pi-embedded-helpers.isbillingerrormessage.test.ts`\\r\\n- `corepack pnpm vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/agents/auth-profiles.markauthprofilefailure.test.ts`\\r\\n- `corepack pnpm vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/state-observation.test.ts`\\r\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56683/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682\",\"id\":4162072858,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874FDEa\",\"number\":56682,\"title\":\"[Bug]: webchat session context lost after Gateway restart (SIGUSR1)\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"lyk-gif\",\"id\":226474448,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODX-50A\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/226474448?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/lyk-gif\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lyk-gif/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:39:15Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:39:15Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nWhen the Gateway restarts (via SIGUSR1 / config.patch), the webchat channel loses its session context entirely. A new conversation is started instead of resuming the previous one.\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter a hot restart (SIGUSR1), the webchat session should either:\\n- Resume the existing conversation context, or\\n- At minimum, re-inject the session history so the agent can continue without losing context\\n\\n## Actual Behavior\\n\\nAfter restart, webchat opens a brand new session with no memory of previous conversation. The user has to re-explain context from scratch.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Other channels (QQBot, Telegram, etc.) can recover via platform-side message history\\n- webchat has no such mechanism, making it uniquely affected\\n- SIGUSR1 hot restart should ideally preserve in-process session state\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- OpenClaw version: 2026.3.24\\n- Channel: webchat\\n- OS: Linux (Ubuntu)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56682/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681\",\"id\":4162048628,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E9J0\",\"number\":56681,\"title\":\"[Bug]: docker version update reports \\\"requires BuildKit. Refer to https://docs.docker.com/go/buildkit/ to learn how to build images with BuildKit enabled\\\"\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"zhanghui-china\",\"id\":63148804,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMTQ4ODA0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63148804?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/zhanghui-china\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/zhanghui-china/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244967,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Something isn't working\"},{\"id\":10313822852,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACZsByhA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/regression\",\"name\":\"regression\",\"color\":\"D93F0B\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Behavior that previously worked and now fails\"}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:24:18Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:34:33Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nOrigin Version:\\n v2026.3.8\\n\\nTarget Version:\\n v2026.3.24\\n\\ndocker install reports \\n`Step 21/64 : RUN --mount=type=cache,id=openclaw-pnpm-store,target=/root/.local/share/pnpm/store,sharing=locked     NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2048 pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\\nthe --mount option requires BuildKit. Refer to https://docs.docker.com/go/buildkit/ to learn how to build images with BuildKit enabled`\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. git checkout v2026.3.24\\n2. ./docker-setup.sh\\n\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\ndocker install/upgrade success\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\n`(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ ./docker-setup.sh\\nDocker Compose not available (try: docker compose version)\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ vi docker-setup.sh\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ vi ./scripts/docker/setup.sh\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ ./docker-setup.sh\\nReusing gateway token from /home/zhanghui/.openclaw/openclaw.json\\n==> Building Docker image: openclaw:local\\nDEPRECATED: The legacy builder is deprecated and will be removed in a future release.\\n            Install the buildx component to build images with BuildKit:\\n            https://docs.docker.com/go/buildx/\\n\\nSending build context to Docker daemon  90.89MB\\nStep 1/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_EXTENSIONS=\\\"\\\"\\nStep 2/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_VARIANT=default\\nStep 3/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_DOCKER_APT_UPGRADE=1\\nStep 4/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_IMAGE=\\\"node:24-bookworm@sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\\"\\nStep 5/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_DIGEST=\\\"sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\\"\\nStep 6/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_SLIM_IMAGE=\\\"node:24-bookworm-slim@sha256:e8e2e91b1378f83c5b2dd15f0247f34110e2fe895f6ca7719dbb780f929368eb\\\"\\nStep 7/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_SLIM_DIGEST=\\\"sha256:e8e2e91b1378f83c5b2dd15f0247f34110e2fe895f6ca7719dbb780f929368eb\\\"\\nStep 8/64 : FROM ${OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_IMAGE} AS ext-deps\\ndocker.io/library/node:24-bookworm@sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b: Pulling from library/node\\n8578011282ae: Already exists\\n443d4217b87a: Already exists\\na3d27b842bb7: Already exists\\n869fdd20a733: Already exists\\n3498e5a179b7: Pull complete\\n628c149e1e33: Pull complete\\n0587cdf2b672: Pull complete\\n36039b6ce9ba: Pull complete\\nDigest: sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\nStatus: Downloaded newer image for node:24-bookworm@sha256:3a09aa6354567619221ef6c45a5051b671f953f0a1924d1f819ffb236e520e6b\\n ---> 736b6f1038f3\\nStep 9/64 : ARG OPENCLAW_EXTENSIONS\\n ---> Running in 4f08c923c82e\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 4f08c923c82e\\n ---> 51ef7e7e9a83\\nStep 10/64 : COPY extensions /tmp/extensions\\n ---> 1e8069fdc197\\nStep 11/64 : RUN mkdir -p /out &&     for ext in $OPENCLAW_EXTENSIONS; do       if [ -f \\\"/tmp/extensions/$ext/package.json\\\" ]; then         mkdir -p \\\"/out/$ext\\\" &&         cp \\\"/tmp/extensions/$ext/package.json\\\" \\\"/out/$ext/package.json\\\";       fi;     done\\n ---> Running in ce15808274e6\\n ---> Removed intermediate container ce15808274e6\\n ---> 40063595b218\\nStep 12/64 : FROM ${OPENCLAW_NODE_BOOKWORM_IMAGE} AS build\\n ---> 736b6f1038f3\\nStep 13/64 : RUN set -eux;     for attempt in 1 2 3 4 5; do       if curl --retry 5 --retry-all-errors --retry-delay 2 -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash; then         break;       fi;       if [ \\\"$attempt\\\" -eq 5 ]; then         exit 1;       fi;       sleep $((attempt * 2));     done\\n ---> Running in 33d9e4c5ca12\\n+ curl --retry 5 --retry-all-errors --retry-delay 2 -fsSL https://bun.sh/install\\n+ bash\\n######################################################################## 100.0%\\nbun was installed successfully to ~/.bun/bin/bun\\n\\nAdded \\\"~/.bun/bin\\\" to $PATH in \\\"~/.bashrc\\\"\\n\\nTo get started, run:\\n\\n  source /root/.bashrc\\n  bun --help\\n+ break\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 33d9e4c5ca12\\n ---> 3396f108ffae\\nStep 14/64 : ENV PATH=\\\"/root/.bun/bin:${PATH}\\\"\\n ---> Running in f8fe9c1c127e\\n ---> Removed intermediate container f8fe9c1c127e\\n ---> d05ac185dd65\\nStep 15/64 : RUN corepack enable\\n ---> Running in 69f67d16a322\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 69f67d16a322\\n ---> 8c5320b11edf\\nStep 16/64 : WORKDIR /app\\n ---> Running in 232c8f726c35\\n ---> Removed intermediate container 232c8f726c35\\n ---> 1074fdb07340\\nStep 17/64 : COPY package.json pnpm-lock.yaml pnpm-workspace.yaml .npmrc ./\\n ---> 51f1c8d99d22\\nStep 18/64 : COPY ui/package.json ./ui/package.json\\n ---> 7851f77e100e\\nStep 19/64 : COPY patches ./patches\\n ---> b1128caeece7\\nStep 20/64 : COPY --from=ext-deps /out/ ./extensions/\\n ---> 2e21e8a90726\\nStep 21/64 : RUN --mount=type=cache,id=openclaw-pnpm-store,target=/root/.local/share/pnpm/store,sharing=locked     NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2048 pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\\nthe --mount option requires BuildKit. Refer to https://docs.docker.com/go/buildkit/ to learn how to build images with BuildKit enabled\\n(base) zhanghui@ubuntu:/home1/zhanghui/openclaw$ `\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\nv2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nubuntu 20.04\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\ndocker\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nz.ai\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nopenclaw->z.ai->coding Plan\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56681/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680\",\"id\":4162040751,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E7Ov\",\"number\":56680,\"title\":\"[Bug]: TTS directive parser treats inline literal [[tts:...]] / [[tts:text]]...[[/tts:text]] examples as active directives\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"scottdownes\",\"id\":8439733,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjg0Mzk3MzM=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8439733?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/scottdownes\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/scottdownes/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244967,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Something isn't working\"}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:19:12Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:52:34Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nparseTtsDirectives() appears to parse TTS tags too broadly. Literal inline mentions of:\\n\\n• [[tts:...]]\\n• [[tts:text]]...[[/tts:text]]\\n\\ninside otherwise ordinary assistant text can be interpreted as active TTS directives instead of plain text examples.\\n\\nIn my case this surfaced on Telegram, where a normal text reply could unexpectedly enter the TTS/audio path.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Configure OpenClaw with TTS enabled on a messaging channel such as Telegram.\\n2. Send a normal assistant reply that includes literal inline examples of TTS tags inside ordinary prose, for example:\\nThis reply mentions [[tts:voice=Audrey]] and [[tts:text]]hello[[/tts:text]] as plain text examples.\\n3. Observe how OpenClaw parses and delivers the reply.\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nThe reply should remain plain text.\\nThe inline tag examples should be treated as literal text, not as active TTS directives.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nThe inline literal TTS examples can be interpreted as active directives, causing the reply to enter the TTS/audio path unexpectedly.\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nLinux 6.8.0-106-generic (x64)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Model\\n\\ngpt-5.4\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nTelegram → local OpenClaw gateway → main agent (gpt-5.4) → TTS directive parser in src/tts/directives.ts\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56680/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679\",\"id\":4162040623,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E7Mv\",\"number\":56679,\"title\":\"Feature request: Allow baseUrl override for built-in providers (anthropic, openai, etc.)\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mids-neo\",\"id\":117532760,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBwFoWA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117532760?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mids-neo\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mids-neo/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:19:07Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:19:07Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Use Case\\n\\nI want to route Anthropic API calls through a local usage-tracking proxy (`localhost:18795`) that captures exact token counts, costs, and rate limit utilization from every API call before forwarding to `api.anthropic.com`.\\n\\nThis is for cost tracking and monitoring — the proxy logs usage to a database, then returns the response unchanged.\\n\\n## What I Tried\\n\\n### Attempt 1: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` env var\\nSet in `openclaw.json` `env` section. OpenClaw ignores it — the gateway has its own Anthropic client that doesn't read this env var.\\n\\n### Attempt 2: `models.providers.anthropic` with empty models\\n```json\\n\\\"models\\\": {\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"merge\\\",\\n  \\\"providers\\\": {\\n    \\\"anthropic\\\": {\\n      \\\"baseUrl\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:18795\\\",\\n      \\\"models\\\": []\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\nConfig validates, gateway writes to `models.json`, but built-in anthropic models ignore the custom baseUrl. Zero traffic routed through the proxy.\\n\\n### Attempt 3: Full model list with `api: \\\"anthropic-messages\\\"`\\n```json\\n\\\"models\\\": {\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"merge\\\",\\n  \\\"providers\\\": {\\n    \\\"anthropic\\\": {\\n      \\\"baseUrl\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:18795\\\",\\n      \\\"api\\\": \\\"anthropic-messages\\\",\\n      \\\"models\\\": [\\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"claude-opus-4-6\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Claude Opus 4.6\\\", \\\"contextWindow\\\": 1000000, \\\"maxTokens\\\": 32768}\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\nConfig validates, container restarted, but still zero proxy traffic. The built-in anthropic provider is not overridden by a custom provider with the same name.\\n\\n## Requested Feature\\n\\nA way to override the `baseUrl` for a built-in provider without re-declaring all its models. For example:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"models\\\": {\\n  \\\"providerOverrides\\\": {\\n    \\\"anthropic\\\": {\\n      \\\"baseUrl\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:18795\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nOr allow the existing `models.providers.anthropic.baseUrl` to actually override the built-in URL when `mode: \\\"merge\\\"` is set.\\n\\n## Environment\\n- OpenClaw version: 2026.3.23-2\\n- Auth method: Anthropic token (Claude Max)\\n- OS: Linux (Docker container)\\n\\n## Workaround\\nCurrently using periodic probe API calls to capture rate limit headers, but this doesn't give per-request cost tracking. An iptables redirect would work but requires TLS termination in the proxy.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56679/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678\",\"id\":4162039699,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU66Y\",\"number\":56678,\"title\":\"fix: normalize openai-codex and github-copilot provider IDs for media-understanding\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"YoungMoneyInvestments\",\"id\":146381908,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCLmcVA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146381908?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/YoungMoneyInvestments\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/YoungMoneyInvestments/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106648,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20S\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:18:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:22:17Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56678\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56678.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen using `openai-codex` (Codex OAuth) or `github-copilot` as a provider, the image/media-understanding tool fails with:\\n\\n> No media-understanding provider registered for openai-codex\\n\\nBoth providers route through OpenAI models that fully support vision, but `normalizeMediaProviderId()` did not map them to `\\\"openai\\\"`, so the registry lookup couldn't find the OpenAI media-understanding adapter.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`src/media-understanding/provider-id.ts`** — Added normalization rules: `openai-codex → openai` and `github-copilot → openai`, matching the existing `gemini → google` pattern.\\n- **`src/media-understanding/provider-registry.test.ts`** — Added two tests confirming both provider variants resolve to the `openai` media-understanding provider.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] All 5 existing + new media-understanding tests pass (`pnpm vitest src/media-understanding`)\\n- [x] Pre-commit hooks (lint, typecheck) pass\\n- [ ] Manual verification: configure `openai-codex` as primary provider → image tool should work without fallback\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56678/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677\",\"id\":4162033640,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU53G\",\"number\":56677,\"title\":\"fix(slack): enforce streaming mode mutual exclusion + guard stream teardown\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"hsiaoa\",\"id\":70124331,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTI0MzMx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70124331?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hsiaoa\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298398,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EBng\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/channel:%20slack\",\"name\":\"channel: slack\",\"color\":\"1d76db\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Channel integration: slack\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:14:41Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:17:00Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56677\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56677.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"Fixes #56675\\nRelated: #54469, #23791\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSlack has three independent streaming mechanisms (native streaming, draft preview, block streaming) that can be active simultaneously, causing duplicate message delivery. Only one mutual exclusion rule was enforced:\\n\\n```\\nNative streaming ON → block streaming OFF  ✅ (already existed)\\nDraft preview ON → block streaming OFF     ❌ (not enforced)\\n```\\n\\nWhen draft preview and block streaming run together:\\n1. Block replies arrive as separate messages\\n2. Draft preview gets finalized via `chat.update` into a permanent message\\n3. User sees the same content twice\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nTwo changes in `dispatch.ts`:\\n\\n### 1. Enforce mutual exclusion: draft preview → disable block streaming\\n\\n```typescript\\ndisableBlockStreaming: useStreaming\\n  ? true\\n  : previewStreamingEnabled\\n    ? true  // NEW: draft preview ON → no block streaming\\n    : typeof account.config.blockStreaming === \\\"boolean\\\"\\n      ? !account.config.blockStreaming\\n      : undefined,\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Guard `stopSlackStream` against unflushed state\\n\\nWhen the stream session exists but the streamer was never initialized (e.g., `startStream` failed), `stopSlackStream` would attempt to start a new stream to flush the buffer. Now checks `finalStream.streamer` before calling stop.\\n\\n## What this does NOT fix (separate PRs needed)\\n\\n- #52536 — Thread target for streaming (needs `thread_ts` plumbing change)\\n- #50976 — Multi-agent streaming routing (needs session scoping)\\n- #55445 — Bolt middleware self-filter (needs middleware change)\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Zero type errors\\n- Backward compatible: configs that only use one streaming mode are unaffected\\n- Configs that accidentally enabled both modes now get correct single-mode behavior\\n\\n## AI Disclosure\\n\\n🤖 AI-assisted (Kiro CLI).\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56677/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676\",\"id\":4162030543,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E4vP\",\"number\":56676,\"title\":\"[Bug]: read tool allowed in config but not executed; agent narrates/fakes read output in Telegram and direct CLI\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"sportsman821\",\"id\":255430270,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODzmOfg\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/255430270?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sportsman821\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sportsman821/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":9706244967,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Something isn't working\"},{\"id\":10319842798,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACZxxN7g\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/bug:behavior\",\"name\":\"bug:behavior\",\"color\":\"D73A4A\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Incorrect behavior without a crash\"}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:13:12Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:13:21Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nOpenClaw is not executing the `read` tool in my setup even though `read` is allowed in config, the target file exists, and memory is healthy. Instead, the agent narrates tool use or returns fabricated content.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n* OpenClaw version: `2026.3.24`\\n* Install type: Docker\\n* Host: Apple Silicon Mac mini M4, 16GB RAM\\n* Container name: `openclaw-worker`\\n* Persistent data mount: `/Users/Shared/openclaw_data:/home/node/.openclaw`\\n* Primary local provider: Ollama\\n* Models tested:\\n\\n  * `ollama/llama3.2:3b`\\n  * `ollama/qwen3.5:9b`\\n  * `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`\\n\\n## Relevant config\\n\\nTools:\\n\\n* profile: `minimal`\\n* allow:\\n\\n  * `read`\\n  * `write`\\n  * `edit`\\n  * `web_search`\\n\\nMemory:\\n\\n* `agents.defaults.memorySearch.enabled = true`\\n* `agents.defaults.memorySearch.provider = ollama`\\n\\n## Health checks\\n\\n`openclaw health`:\\n\\n* Telegram ok\\n* agent main ok\\n\\n`openclaw memory status --deep`:\\n\\n* Provider: `ollama`\\n* Model: `nomic-embed-text`\\n* Embeddings: `ready`\\n* Indexed: `4/4 files`\\n* Dirty: `no`\\n\\n## Target file\\n\\nThe file exists in-container and is readable:\\n\\nPath:\\n`/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md`\\n\\nVerified output:\\n\\n```text\\nexists: True\\nsize: 1574\\n--- first 3 lines ---\\n01: # 2026-03-27\\n02:\\n03: ## Session Notes\\n```\\n\\n## Repro prompt\\n\\n```text\\nUse the read tool on /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md and quote exactly the first bullet under \\\"## Session Notes\\\".\\n```\\n\\n## Expected result\\n\\n```text\\nRefactored workspace into a lean production structure\\n```\\n\\n## Actual results\\n\\n### Telegram with `ollama/llama3.2:3b`\\n\\nReturned fabricated content:\\n\\n```text\\n# Memory\\n- The current time is Saturday, March 28th, 2026.\\n```\\n\\n### Telegram with `ollama/qwen3.5:9b`\\n\\nNarrated tool use and returned wrong content:\\n\\n```text\\nread /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md\\n...\\nThe current time is Saturday, March 28th, 2026.\\n```\\n\\n### Telegram with `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`\\n\\nAdmitted it could not use `read` in that chat path:\\n\\n```text\\nI can’t directly use a read tool from within this chat...\\n```\\n\\n### Direct CLI path\\n\\nCommand:\\n\\n```bash\\ndocker exec -it openclaw-worker openclaw agent \\\\\\n  --message 'Use the read tool on /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md and quote exactly the first bullet under \\\"## Session Notes\\\".' \\\\\\n  --session-id direct-read-test \\\\\\n  --timeout 120\\n```\\n\\nReturned wrong content:\\n\\n```text\\nI will run `read` on `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md`.\\n\\nThe output is:\\n> * No new tasks assigned today. HEARTBEAT_OK\\n```\\n\\nAfter switching that path to `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`, it still returned wrong content:\\n\\n```text\\nI will run `read` on `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-27.md`.\\n\\nThe output is:\\n> * User mentioned a possible new skill: \\\"node-connect\\\" for debugging OpenClaw node connection and pairing issues.\\n```\\n\\n## Session evidence\\n\\nThe saved session transcript records assistant text and `model-snapshot` custom events, but I could not find evidence of an actual read-tool execution event in the failed session.\\n\\nObserved event types in one failed session:\\n\\n```text\\n3  custom\\n9  message\\n1  session\\n1  thinking_level_change\\n```\\n\\nThe `custom` events in that session were `model-snapshot` only.\\n\\n## Why I think this is a bug\\n\\nI believe this is not a memory indexing issue and not just a weak-model issue, because:\\n\\n* `read` is explicitly allowed\\n* the file exists and is readable inside the container\\n* memory search is enabled\\n* embeddings are ready\\n* indexing is complete (`4/4 files`)\\n* the issue reproduces in both Telegram and direct CLI\\n* the issue reproduces with both local and remote models\\n\\n## Question\\n\\nIs this a known tool-routing / tool-execution issue in the agent path, or is there another config/runtime requirement for enabling actual `read` tool execution in Telegram and direct CLI sessions?\\n\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\nSee explanation above\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nAgent can read and output results from a daily memory file.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nHallucination/generic model output\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nmacOS 15.4\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Model\\n\\n  * `ollama/llama3.2:3b`   * `ollama/qwen3.5:9b`   * `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nDocker container (`ghcr.io/openclaw/openclaw:2026.3.24`) on Apple Silicon Mac mini M4 → OpenClaw gateway/agent runtime (`openclaw-worker`) → model provider selected per session:  * Local path tested:    * OpenClaw → Ollama → `llama3.2:3b`   * OpenClaw → Ollama → `qwen3.5:9b`  * Remote path tested:    * OpenClaw → OpenAI Codex → `gpt-5.4`  Affected interaction paths:  * Telegram bot session * Direct CLI via `openclaw agent`  No extra reverse proxy or external model router in front of OpenClaw. Persistent state is mounted from `/Users/Shared/openclaw_data` to `/home/node/.openclaw`.\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56676/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675\",\"id\":4162028905,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874E4Vp\",\"number\":56675,\"title\":\"Slack streaming: mutual exclusion between streaming modes causes duplicate delivery, stale previews, and thread misrouting\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"hsiaoa\",\"id\":70124331,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTI0MzMx\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70124331?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hsiaoa\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hsiaoa/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:12:16Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:12:16Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nSlack has three independent streaming mechanisms that can be active simultaneously, causing a class of bugs where content is delivered twice, previews are never cleaned up, or streams land in the wrong thread. Six open issues trace back to this root cause.\\n\\n## The Problem\\n\\nThe three streaming layers:\\n\\n| Mode | Mechanism | Config |\\n|------|-----------|--------|\\n| **Native streaming** | `chat.startStream`/`appendStream`/`stopStream` | `streaming: partial` + `nativeStreaming: true` |\\n| **Draft preview** | `sendMessage` + `chat.update` edits | `streaming: partial` + `nativeStreaming: false` |\\n| **Block streaming** | Separate messages per completed text block | `blockStreaming: true` (channel or agent default) |\\n\\nCurrently, only ONE mutual exclusion rule is enforced:\\n\\n```\\nNative streaming ON → disableBlockStreaming = true  ✅\\n```\\n\\nThe other two are NOT enforced:\\n\\n```\\nBlock streaming ON → draft preview should be disabled  ❌ not enforced\\nDraft preview ON → block streaming should be disabled  ❌ not enforced\\n```\\n\\nThis means block streaming and draft preview can run simultaneously. When they do:\\n1. Block replies arrive as separate messages\\n2. Draft preview gets finalized via `chat.update` into a permanent message\\n3. User sees the same content twice\\n\\n## Related Issues\\n\\n| Issue | Symptom | Root Cause |\\n|-------|---------|------------|\\n| #54469 | `stopSlackStream` calls `startStream` on unflushed buffer during teardown | Native streaming teardown race — no guard on buffer state |\\n| #52536 | First thread reply streams to channel instead of thread | `thread_ts` not passed to streaming start — thread target resolution happens after stream init |\\n| #42200 | Streaming messages show incomplete content | Draft preview shows only final chunk, not accumulated text |\\n| #23791 | `streaming: false` doesn't disable draft preview | Draft preview not gated by the `streaming` config flag |\\n| #50976 | Multi-agent: `streaming: partial` causes wrong agent to respond | Streaming session not scoped to agent — shared state leaks across agents |\\n| #55445 | `message_changed` events dropped by bot self-filter | Bolt middleware filters the bot's own `chat.update` edits, breaking streaming feedback loop |\\n\\n## Proposed Fix\\n\\nEnforce mutual exclusion at the dispatch level in `extensions/slack/src/monitor/message-handler/dispatch.ts`:\\n\\n1. **Block streaming ON → disable draft preview finalization.** Check `blockReplyPipeline?.didStream()` before `canFinalizeViaPreviewEdit`. If block replies were sent, clear the draft instead of finalizing it.\\n\\n2. **Draft preview ON → disable block streaming.** When `previewStreamingEnabled=true` and `useStreaming=false`, set `disableBlockStreaming=true` to prevent both running simultaneously.\\n\\n3. **`streaming: off` should mean off.** When `streaming=off`, ensure draft preview is also disabled (fixes #23791). Currently `previewStreamingEnabled` is computed from `slackStreaming.mode !== \\\"off\\\"` but the draft stream is still initialized.\\n\\n4. **Thread target for streaming.** Pass `thread_ts` to `startSlackStream` from the reply plan, not from a separate resolution (fixes #52536).\\n\\n5. **Guard `stopSlackStream` against unflushed state.** Check `streamSession.stopped` and buffer state before calling stop (fixes #54469).\\n\\nThese are all in `dispatch.ts` — single file, same dispatch function. The multi-agent issue (#50976) and self-filter issue (#55445) are separate fixes but benefit from the same cleanup.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- **In scope:** Mutual exclusion enforcement, draft preview cleanup, thread target fix, teardown guard\\n- **Out of scope:** Multi-agent streaming routing (#50976), Bolt middleware self-filter (#55445) — these need separate PRs\\n- **Backward compatible:** No config changes needed. Existing configs that accidentally enable both modes will get correct behavior instead of duplicates.\\n\\n## Prior Art\\n\\n- PR #29887 attempted to disable draft preview when block streaming is off, but was never reviewed.\\n- Discord and Telegram don't have this problem because they use atomic message editing (one API call replaces content), while Slack uses separate add/edit/stream APIs.\\n\\n/cc @steipete @vincentkoc\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56675/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674\",\"id\":4162002889,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU0TP\",\"number\":56674,\"title\":\"feat(openresponses): return reasoning/thinking content in /v1/responses output\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"tonga54\",\"id\":22188504,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg4NTA0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22188504?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/tonga54\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298857,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDaQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/gateway\",\"name\":\"gateway\",\"color\":\"d4c5f9\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Gateway runtime\"},{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106720,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwYA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20M\",\"name\":\"size: M\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:57:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:40:33Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56674\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56674.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- **Problem:** The `/v1/responses` endpoint does not return model reasoning/thinking content. When models produce chain-of-thought reasoning (Anthropic Claude, OpenAI o-series, Gemini thinking, Ollama thinking models), the reasoning output is silently discarded by the HTTP API. Callers have no way to observe model reasoning through the OpenResponses interface.\\n- **Why it matters:** The [Open Responses spec](https://www.openresponses.org/reference) defines `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` as a first-class output item (`ReasoningBody`) and `response.reasoning.delta`/`response.reasoning.done` as streaming events. Not implementing these means OpenClaw's OpenResponses endpoint is incomplete relative to the spec, and API callers (dashboards, orchestrators, observability tools) cannot access reasoning data.\\n- **What changed:** The endpoint now captures reasoning content from agent thinking events and returns it as `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` output items (non-stream) or `response.reasoning.delta`/`response.reasoning.done` SSE events (stream). When no assistant text is produced but reasoning exists, the reasoning text is used as a fallback response to avoid empty replies from thinking-only models.\\n- **What did NOT change (scope boundary):** No config changes required. No new dependencies. Existing behavior for non-reasoning models is unchanged. The `onReasoningStream` callback path for channel-specific reasoning delivery (Discord, Telegram, etc.) is unmodified. This change only adds reasoning to the HTTP API surface.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [ ] Bug fix\\n- [x] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [x] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [x] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Related #54496\\n- Related #44513\\n- Related #8364\\n- [ ] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A — this is a new feature implementing an existing spec item.\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\n### Non-streaming responses\\n\\nWhen reasoning is produced, the response `output` array now includes a `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` item before the assistant message:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"output\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"reasoning_abc123\\\",\\n      \\\"content\\\": \\\"Let me think about this step by step...\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"message\\\",\\n      \\\"role\\\": \\\"assistant\\\",\\n      \\\"content\\\": [{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"output_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"The answer is 42.\\\" }]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Streaming responses\\n\\nTwo new SSE event types are emitted during streaming:\\n\\n- `response.reasoning.delta` — cumulative reasoning text as it streams\\n- `response.reasoning.done` — final reasoning text when complete\\n\\n### Fallback behavior\\n\\nWhen a model produces reasoning but no assistant text (common with thinking-only model configurations), the reasoning content is used as the response text instead of returning \\\"No response from OpenClaw.\\\"\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```\\nModel produces reasoning + answer:\\n\\n  [thinking events] ──→ collect reasoning ──→ output[0]: reasoning item\\n  [assistant events] ──→ collect text     ──→ output[1]: assistant message\\n\\nModel produces reasoning only (no assistant text):\\n\\n  [thinking events] ──→ collect reasoning ──→ output[0]: reasoning item\\n  (no assistant text)                     ──→ output[1]: assistant = reasoning fallback\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? No\\n- Data access scope changed? No — reasoning content was already produced by the model, it was just being discarded\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: macOS 15.4 (Apple Silicon)\\n- Runtime: Node 22, Bun 1.2\\n- Model: any reasoning-capable model (Claude, o-series, Gemini thinking)\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Send a POST to `/v1/responses` with a reasoning-capable model\\n2. Observe the response `output` array\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\nReasoning content appears as `type: \\\"reasoning\\\"` output item.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\nSame as expected.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] `pnpm build` green\\n- [x] `pnpm check` green (lint, format, types)\\n- [x] `src/gateway/openresponses-http.test.ts` — 12/12 tests pass\\n- [x] `src/agents/pi-embedded-subscribe.*` — 21/30 pass (9 pre-existing upstream failures, verified same count on clean `upstream/main`)\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified: non-stream reasoning collection, stream reasoning events, fallback from thinking to text, cleanup on error\\n- Edge cases: no reasoning produced (no-op), reasoning-only response (fallback), tool-call + reasoning combined output\\n- Not verified: production load, all provider-specific thinking formats\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes — adds new output items, does not remove or change existing ones\\n- Config/env changes? No\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: reasoning content could be large (10k+ chars) for complex prompts, increasing response payload size\\n  - Mitigation: This mirrors the model's actual output; callers can ignore the reasoning item if not needed\\n- Risk: double `emitAgentEvent` calls (raw + formatted) for channel-streaming reasoning mode\\n  - Mitigation: The raw-only event fires first for HTTP capture; the formatted event fires only when `streamReasoning` is active. HTTP consumers filter by `rawText` presence.\\n\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56674/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673\",\"id\":4162002533,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OU0Oz\",\"number\":56673,\"title\":\"feat(agents): add opt-in sessions_await tool for parallel sub-agent orchestration\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"tonga54\",\"id\":22188504,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg4NTA0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22188504?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/tonga54\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/tonga54/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106760,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwiA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20L\",\"name\":\"size: L\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:57:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:52:52Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56673\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56673.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- **Problem:** Orchestrator agents that spawn multiple parallel sub-agents have no reliable way to block until all workers complete. The only option today is polling `sessions_list` in a loop, which LLMs do unreliably — they skip ahead with partial results despite prompt engineering.\\n- **Why it matters:** Fan-out/fan-in orchestration (main -> orchestrator -> N workers) is one of the most requested subagent patterns. Without a blocking primitive, orchestrators produce incomplete or inconsistent results.\\n- **What changed:** Adds a `sessions_await` tool and `suppressAnnounce`/`waitForCompletion` parameters to `sessions_spawn`, gated behind `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled` (opt-in, off by default).\\n- **What did NOT change (scope boundary):** No behavioral change for existing users. All new functionality requires explicit config opt-in. Registry, lifecycle, and run-manager internals gain the `suppressAutoAnnounce` field but it is inert unless the config flag is enabled.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [ ] Bug fix\\n- [x] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [x] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [x] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [x] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Closes #31499\\n- Related #38522\\n- Related #30767\\n- [ ] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\nN/A — new feature, not a regression fix.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\nWhen `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled: true` is set in `openclaw.json`:\\n\\n1. A new `sessions_await` tool becomes available to agents, accepting an array of session keys and an optional timeout.\\n2. `sessions_spawn` gains `suppressAnnounce` and `waitForCompletion` boolean parameters.\\n3. The system prompt includes guidance on the spawn+await pattern for parallel work.\\n\\nWhen the flag is unset or false (default): no changes to behavior.\\n\\n### Configuration\\n\\n```jsonc\\n{\\n  \\\"agents\\\": {\\n    \\\"defaults\\\": {\\n      \\\"subagents\\\": {\\n        \\\"awaitEnabled\\\": true\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Usage pattern\\n\\nThe agent spawns multiple workers with `suppressAnnounce: true`, then calls `sessions_await` with all session keys to block until every result is ready:\\n\\n```\\nsessions_spawn(task=\\\"analyze file A\\\", suppressAnnounce=true) -> key1\\nsessions_spawn(task=\\\"analyze file B\\\", suppressAnnounce=true) -> key2\\nsessions_await(sessionKeys=[key1, key2], timeoutSeconds=300)\\n-> { status: \\\"ok\\\", results: [{ key1, reply: \\\"...\\\" }, { key2, reply: \\\"...\\\" }] }\\n```\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```\\n                       ┌─────────────┐\\n                       │ Parent Agent │\\n                       └──────┬──────┘\\n                              │\\n            ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐\\n            │ spawn(suppress) │ spawn(suppress)  │\\n            ▼                 │                  ▼\\n     ┌──────────┐             │           ┌──────────┐\\n     │ Worker 1 │             │           │ Worker 2 │\\n     └────┬─────┘             │           └────┬─────┘\\n          │                   │                │\\n          ▼                   ▼                ▼\\n       complete    sessions_await([k1,k2])  complete\\n                         │\\n                         ▼\\n                  { results: [...] }\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No — tools only available when config flag is on\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No — uses existing `agent.wait` gateway RPC\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? Yes — new `sessions_await` tool (gated)\\n- Data access scope changed? No\\n- The tool reads run results already available in the subagent registry; no new data surface is exposed.\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: macOS 15.4 (Apple Silicon)\\n- Runtime: Node 22, Bun 1.2\\n- Model: any model with tool-calling support\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Set `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled: true` in `openclaw.json`\\n2. Ask the agent to \\\"analyze files A, B, and C in parallel\\\"\\n3. Agent spawns 3 workers with `suppressAnnounce: true`\\n4. Agent calls `sessions_await` with all 3 session keys\\n5. All results collected before agent responds\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\nAgent blocks until all 3 workers complete, then synthesizes a combined response.\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\nSame as expected.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] Passing scoped tests: `sessions-await-tool.test.ts` (4/4), `announce-loop-guard.test.ts` (6/6)\\n- [x] `pnpm build` green\\n- [x] `pnpm check` green (lint, format, types, all boundary checks)\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified: tool registration gated behind config flag, system prompt conditional on tool presence, spawn params only exposed when flag is on\\n- Edge cases: empty keys, unknown keys, timeout, mixed completed/active/unknown sessions\\n- Not verified: multi-gateway distributed scenario, production load\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes — off by default, zero behavioral change without opt-in\\n- Config/env changes? Yes — new optional `agents.defaults.subagents.awaitEnabled` boolean\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: `sessions_await` could hold an agent turn open for the full timeout duration if workers stall\\n  - Mitigation: Configurable timeout (default 300s), partial results returned on timeout\\n- Risk: `suppressAutoAnnounce` could silently drop completion messages if `sessions_await` is never called\\n  - Mitigation: Only set when explicitly requested via tool param; existing announce flow is the default\\n\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56673/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672\",\"id\":4162001032,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUz7Q\",\"number\":56672,\"title\":\"feat: fire session_end hook on subagent completion and cron session end\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mitchelldavis44\",\"id\":6354781,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3ODE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6354781?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mitchelldavis44\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mitchelldavis44/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:56:56Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:18:39Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56672\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56672.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nExtends the `session_end` plugin hook to fire in two additional lifecycle cases that were previously missing.\\n\\n### Problem\\n\\nThe `session_end` hook only fired on session reset/replace (one narrow path in `session.ts`). This made it impossible for plugins to react to task completion without polling — blocking use cases like dispatch queues, memory consolidation, and post-session cleanup.\\n\\nTracked in:\\n- Fixes #10142 (session:end event for workflow integration)\\n- Related to #31266 (session-memory hook wanting session:end)\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n**`src/agents/subagent-spawn.ts`**\\n- Fires `session_end` alongside the existing `subagent_ended` hook when a subagent completes\\n- Guarded with `hookRunner?.hasHooks('session_end')` — zero overhead if no listeners\\n- Uses `buildSessionEndHookPayload` for consistent payload shape\\n\\n**`src/cron/isolated-agent/run.ts`**\\n- Fires `session_end` after the cron isolated agent session completes and session entry is persisted\\n- Same guard pattern\\n\\n**`src/plugins/types.ts`**\\n- Updated `session_end` comment to document all three trigger cases: session reset/replace, subagent completion, cron completion\\n\\n**`CHANGELOG.md`**\\n- Added entry under Unreleased\\n\\n### Backward Compatibility\\n\\n- `subagent_ended` hook continues to fire alongside `session_end` — no breaking change\\n- All new calls are opt-in via the existing `hasHooks` guard\\n\\n### Motivation\\n\\nThis unblocks the [openclaw-dispatch](https://clawhub.com) plugin (currently in development) which needs to know when sessions complete to drain a task queue without heartbeat polling.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56672/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671\",\"id\":4161995997,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUy9u\",\"number\":56671,\"title\":\"fix(config): deduplicate clobbered config snapshots in-process\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:54:38Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:57:26Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56671\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56671.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n`openclaw doctor --fix` generates **thousands** of timestamped `.clobbered.*` backup files instead of one, filling up the config directory.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nConfirmed by @martingarramon in #56450:\\n\\n`writeConfigHealthState` in `src/config/io.ts` is wrapped in a silent `catch {}`. When the health state file can't be written during the config directory migration that `doctor --fix` triggers, the dedup signature (`lastObservedSuspiciousSignature`) is never persisted to disk. Every subsequent `readConfigFile` call sees no prior signature and calls `persistClobberedConfigSnapshot` unconditionally, generating one timestamped file per read.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nAdded an in-process `Set<string>` (`observedSuspiciousSignatures`) that tracks config anomaly signatures within the current process lifecycle. Both code paths now check this Set before writing a clobbered snapshot:\\n\\n- **Async path** (`observeConfigSnapshot`): dedup check added before `persistClobberedConfigSnapshot`\\n- **Sync path** (`observeConfigSnapshotSync`): same dedup check added\\n\\nThis ensures that even when the on-disk health state fails to persist, the same signature is only processed once per process.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `src/config/io.ts`\\n\\nFixes #56450\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56671/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670\",\"id\":4161995129,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874EwF5\",\"number\":56670,\"title\":\"openai-completions streaming: token usage always zero in session files\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"teo-cc\",\"id\":269157512,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOEAsEiA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269157512?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/teo-cc\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/teo-cc/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:54:02Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:54:02Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nWhen using the `openai-completions` API provider (via LiteLLM proxy to llama-server), all assistant messages in session files record zero token usage:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"usage\\\": {\\\"input\\\": 0, \\\"output\\\": 0, \\\"cacheRead\\\": 0, \\\"cacheWrite\\\": 0, \\\"totalTokens\\\": 0}\\n```\\n\\nThis breaks auto-compaction, which relies on `estimateContextTokens()` → `shouldCompact()` to detect when context is full. With zero usage, compaction never triggers and the model silently loses context.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n- **Auto-compaction never fires** — `shouldCompact(0, 65536, {reserveTokens: 16384})` → false\\n- **Long-running tasks fail silently** — the model hits context limits, loses the original task instruction, and stops mid-work (produces `stopReason: \\\"stop\\\"` instead of continuing)\\n- In our case: a 40+ PR review task stopped after 8 PRs because the 65K context filled up with no compaction\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- OpenClaw **2026.3.24**\\n- pi-ai with OpenAI SDK **6.26.0**\\n- Provider: LiteLLM proxy (`openai-completions` API)\\n- Backend: llama-server (llama.cpp) serving Qwen3.5-35B-A3B\\n- Model config: `contextWindow: 65536`, `maxTokens: 8192`, `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"`\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nAll three layers correctly report token usage:\\n\\n1. **llama-server** returns correct usage in streaming responses (verified with curl)\\n2. **LiteLLM** passes usage through in both streaming (`stream_options.include_usage`) and non-streaming modes (verified with curl)\\n3. **OpenAI Node SDK 6.26.0** correctly exposes `chunk.usage` on the final streaming chunk (verified with a direct Node.js test using the same SDK from the OpenClaw installation)\\n\\nDespite this, session files consistently show zero usage for ALL sessions using `openai-completions`.\\n\\n## Contrast: `anthropic-messages` works\\n\\nOlder sessions using `api: anthropic-messages` (GitHub Copilot with Claude models) record correct usage:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"usage\\\": {\\\"input\\\": 3, \\\"output\\\": 18, \\\"cacheRead\\\": 0, \\\"cacheWrite\\\": 11258, \\\"totalTokens\\\": 11279}\\n```\\n\\nThe issue is specific to the `openai-completions` streaming code path.\\n\\n## Code analysis\\n\\nTraced through the full code path in compiled JS:\\n\\n1. `buildParams()` sets `stream_options: { include_usage: true }` (line 299, `openai-completions.js`) — confirmed via `detectCompat` defaulting `supportsUsageInStreaming: true`\\n2. `parseChunkUsage()` (line 618) correctly parses `prompt_tokens`/`completion_tokens` from raw usage\\n3. The streaming loop (line 96) checks `chunk.usage` before processing choices\\n4. `output.usage` is set before `stream.push({ type: \\\"done\\\", message: output })`\\n5. Lazy-loaded `forwardStream` forwards events including \\\"done\\\" to the outer stream\\n6. `agentLoop` → `streamAssistantResponse` calls `response.result()` for the final message\\n7. `Agent._processLoopEvent` emits `message_end` with the message\\n8. `AgentSession._processAgentEvent` calls `sessionManager.appendMessage(event.message)`\\n\\nEvery step looks correct in static analysis. The bug is likely a subtle async timing issue in the lazy-loaded stream forwarding or the EventStream's push/done/result interaction, but requires runtime instrumentation to pinpoint.\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nNone effective. Increasing context window delays the problem but doesn't fix it. Manual `/compact` works but defeats the purpose of auto-compaction for long autonomous tasks.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n`openai-completions` sessions should record non-zero `usage.input`, `usage.output`, and `usage.totalTokens` from the streaming response, matching the values returned by the upstream provider.\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":1},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56670/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669\",\"id\":4161991851,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUyQZ\",\"number\":56669,\"title\":\"fix(tools): preserve Optional annotation when merging anyOf variants in normalizeToolParameters\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:51:55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:56:01Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56669\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56669.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nThe `message` tool schema declares `buttons` as a required parameter (`required: [\\\"action\\\", \\\"buttons\\\"]`), causing all non-send actions (react, delete, edit, poll) to fail with validation error unless an empty `buttons: []` array is passed.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n`normalizeToolParameters()` in `src/agents/pi-tools.schema.ts` flattens `anyOf` variants into a merged `Type.Object`. During that merge, the TypeBox `Optional` annotation (`Symbol.for('TypeBox.Optional')`) on properties like `buttons` is preserved in the property schema value but not consulted when computing the merged `required` array. Since `buttons` appears in every variant's required list (after the Optional marker is stripped by the variant extraction), it resurfaces as required in the merged output.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nAdded a check in the merged required computation to inspect each property for the TypeBox Optional symbol. Properties annotated as Optional are now excluded from the required array, matching the original schema intent.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `src/agents/pi-tools.schema.ts` — filter Optional-annotated properties from merged required\\n\\nFixes #56496\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56669/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668\",\"id\":4161988082,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUxnX\",\"number\":56668,\"title\":\"fix(gateway): add WebSocket ping keepalive to prevent idle connection drops\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"joelagnel\",\"id\":37460,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NDYw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37460?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/joelagnel\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/joelagnel/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298857,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDaQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/gateway\",\"name\":\"gateway\",\"color\":\"d4c5f9\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Gateway runtime\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:49:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:51:23Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56668\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56668.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Problem: WebSocket webchat connections silently drop (close code 1006) during long tool call chains because the server sends zero WS-level ping frames. Network intermediaries treat the connection as idle and kill it.\\n- Why it matters: Users lose live message delivery during tool execution; buffered messages only flood in when a new connection opens on next user action.\\n- What changed: Added a 25s server-side WebSocket ping interval per connection in the gateway WS handler, cleared on close.\\n- What did NOT change (scope boundary): No client-side changes, no new config options, no protocol changes. The existing application-level tick broadcast is untouched.\\n\\n## Change Type (select all)\\n\\n- [x] Bug fix\\n- [ ] Feature\\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\\n- [ ] Docs\\n- [ ] Security hardening\\n- [ ] Chore/infra\\n\\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\\n\\n- [x] Gateway / orchestration\\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\\n- [ ] Memory / storage\\n- [ ] Integrations\\n- [ ] API / contracts\\n- [ ] UI / DX\\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\\n\\n## Linked Issue/PR\\n\\n- Closes #56645\\n- Related #40063\\n- [x] This PR fixes a bug or regression\\n\\n## Root Cause / Regression History (if applicable)\\n\\n- Root cause: The gateway WebSocketServer never calls `socket.ping()`. The existing keepalive is an application-level JSON `\\\"tick\\\"` event broadcast (every 30s), which is a regular data frame — not a WS protocol ping. Some intermediaries only honor WS-level ping/pong for idle detection. Additionally, the tick broadcast uses `dropIfSlow: true`, so slow clients can miss ticks entirely, leaving the connection truly idle.\\n- Missing detection / guardrail: No WS ping/pong was ever implemented server-side.\\n- Prior context: The `TICK_INTERVAL_MS` application-level keepalive was the only mechanism; WS-level pings were never added.\\n- Why this regressed now: Not a regression — this was never implemented. Became visible with longer tool call chains that create 30-60s idle windows.\\n- If unknown, what was ruled out: N/A\\n\\n## Regression Test Plan (if applicable)\\n\\n- Coverage level that should have caught this:\\n  - [ ] Unit test\\n  - [ ] Seam / integration test\\n  - [ ] End-to-end test\\n  - [x] Existing coverage already sufficient\\n- If no new test is added, why not: The fix is a single `setInterval` + `clearInterval` — the 20 existing ws-connection tests pass and verify connection lifecycle. The actual bug (intermediary killing idle connections) is a network-level behavior not reproducible in unit tests.\\n\\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\\n\\nWebSocket connections now send protocol-level ping frames every 25 seconds, preventing network intermediaries from dropping idle connections during long tool call chains.\\n\\n## Diagram (if applicable)\\n\\n```text\\nBefore:\\n[tool call starts] -> [30-60s idle on WS] -> [intermediary kills connection] -> [user sends msg] -> [new conn] -> [message flood]\\n\\nAfter:\\n[tool call starts] -> [ping every 25s keeps conn alive] -> [messages delivered live]\\n```\\n\\n## Security Impact (required)\\n\\n- New permissions/capabilities? No\\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\\n- New/changed network calls? No (WS ping is a control frame on an existing connection)\\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? No\\n- Data access scope changed? No\\n\\n## Repro + Verification\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: Linux\\n- Runtime/container: Node 22+\\n- Integration/channel (if any): Webchat / Control UI dashboard\\n\\n### Steps\\n\\n1. Open dashboard webchat\\n2. Send a message that triggers multiple tool calls (30-60s)\\n3. Observe: connection stays alive, messages delivered live\\n\\n### Expected\\n\\n- WebSocket connection stays alive during tool execution\\n\\n### Actual\\n\\n- (Before fix) Connection drops silently with code 1006\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- [x] Failing test/log before + passing after\\n- 20/20 existing ws-connection tests pass\\n- Gateway logs from issue show `[ws] webchat disconnected code=1006` — 12 disconnects in 17 minutes\\n\\n## Human Verification (required)\\n\\n- Verified scenarios: All 20 ws-connection tests pass; format check passes\\n- Edge cases checked: `close()` clears the ping interval; `socket.ping()` is wrapped in try/catch for safety\\n- What you did **not** verify: Live network intermediary behavior (requires deployed gateway + real Tailscale/proxy setup)\\n\\n## Review Conversations\\n\\n- [x] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\\n- [x] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\\n\\n## Compatibility / Migration\\n\\n- Backward compatible? Yes\\n- Config/env changes? No\\n- Migration needed? No\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n- Risk: Minimal additional network traffic (one 2-byte ping frame per connection every 25s)\\n  - Mitigation: Standard WS best practice per RFC 6455 §5.5.2; negligible overhead\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56668/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667\",\"id\":4161986434,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUxVP\",\"number\":56667,\"title\":\"fix(mistral): use mistral-conversations API instead of openai-completions\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:48:25Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:53:32Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56667\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nThe Mistral onboarding wizard (`openclaw onboard --auth-choice mistral-api-key`) configured the provider with `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"`, causing every agent request to fail with **HTTP 422** because Mistral rejects OpenAI-specific parameters:\\n\\n- `store: false` → `Extra inputs are not permitted`\\n- `max_completion_tokens` → `Extra inputs are not permitted`\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n`extensions/mistral/onboard.ts` and `extensions/mistral/provider-catalog.ts` both hardcoded `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"`. The codebase already has a native Mistral API (`mistral-conversations`) that uses the official Mistral SDK and sends only parameters Mistral supports, but the onboarding flow wasn't using it.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- `extensions/mistral/onboard.ts`: `api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"` → `\\\"mistral-conversations\\\"`\\n- `extensions/mistral/provider-catalog.ts`: same change\\n- `extensions/mistral/onboard.test.ts`: updated assertions\\n\\nFixes #56546\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56667/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666\",\"id\":4161984593,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUxAo\",\"number\":56666,\"title\":\"fix: use pinned channel registry in outbound adapter loader\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"aliyaredpilled\",\"id\":148153466,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCNSkeg\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148153466?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/aliyaredpilled\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/aliyaredpilled/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:47:21Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:49:08Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56666\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n`createChannelRegistryLoader` (`src/channels/plugins/registry-loader.ts`) used `getActivePluginRegistry()` to look up channel outbound adapters. The active registry can be silently replaced at runtime — for example, when `resolvePluginCapabilityProviders` reloads plugins to search for media-understanding providers upon receiving an inbound media message.\\n\\nThe sibling `getChannelPlugin()` (used for channel resolution checks) already reads from the **pinned** channel registry via `requireActivePluginChannelRegistry()`, which is specifically designed to survive such reloads (see the docstring on `pinActivePluginChannelRegistry` in `src/plugins/runtime.ts`).\\n\\nThis mismatch caused `loadChannelOutboundAdapter` to fail with **\\\"Outbound not configured for channel: telegram\\\"** during agent turns dispatched via the gateway WebSocket RPC (`method: \\\"agent\\\"` with `deliver: true`). The active registry lost the channel plugin entries after a media message triggered a capability-provider reload, while the pinned registry still had them.\\n\\n**Fix:** switch `createChannelRegistryLoader` from `getActivePluginRegistry()` to `requireActivePluginChannelRegistry()`, making the outbound adapter loader consistent with `getChannelPlugin()`.\\n\\n## Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Configure a gateway with two agents — one bound to a Telegram group, another to Max/Telegram DM\\n2. Set a primary model with an expired OAuth token so model fallback is triggered\\n3. Send a media message (image/file) to one of the agents\\n4. Trigger an agent turn to the Telegram-bound agent via WS RPC (`method: \\\"agent\\\"`, `deliver: true`)\\n5. The agent's response fails to deliver with: `Error: Outbound not configured for channel: telegram`\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] Verify `getChannelPlugin(\\\"telegram\\\")` and `loadChannelOutboundAdapter(\\\"telegram\\\")` return consistent results after a capability-provider reload\\n- [ ] Verify agent turn delivery to Telegram groups works after inbound media messages\\n- [ ] Existing channel registry pin tests in `runtime.channel-pin.test.ts` still pass\\n\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56666/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664\",\"id\":4161981842,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUwis\",\"number\":56664,\"title\":\"fix(discord): handle reconnect-exhausted gracefully instead of crashing gateway\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298117,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EAhQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/channel:%20discord\",\"name\":\"channel: discord\",\"color\":\"1d76db\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Channel integration: discord\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:45:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:50:43Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56664\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56664.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen the Discord WebSocket connection drops and reconnection attempts are exhausted (e.g. during health-monitor stale-socket restarts), Carbon fires a `Max reconnect attempts (0)` error. Previously this error propagated as an **uncaught exception that killed the entire gateway process**.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nThree code paths in `provider.lifecycle.ts` did not handle `reconnect-exhausted` events outside of the shutdown context:\\n\\n1. **`handleGatewayEvent`**: Only suppressed `reconnect-exhausted` when `lifecycleStopping` was true. During a health-monitor stale-socket restart, `lifecycleStopping` is false, so the event fell through to the generic error handler with `shouldStopLifecycle: true`.\\n\\n2. **`drainPendingGatewayErrors`**: Only suppressed `reconnect-exhausted` during shutdown (`lifecycleStopping || abortSignal.aborted`). Outside shutdown, it threw `event.err` as an exception.\\n\\n3. **`catch` block**: Only caught `disallowed-intents` errors. Any `reconnect-exhausted` error from `waitForDiscordGatewayStop` was re-thrown, becoming an uncaught exception.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`handleGatewayEvent`**: Now handles `reconnect-exhausted` in all scenarios — logs at info level during shutdown, logs at error level otherwise, and always returns `\\\"stop\\\"` instead of letting the error propagate\\n- **`drainPendingGatewayErrors`**: Treats `reconnect-exhausted` unconditionally as a stop-without-throw event (same as `disallowed-intents`)\\n- **`catch` block**: Catches `reconnect-exhausted` errors and logs them instead of re-throwing\\n\\nThe Discord channel lifecycle stops gracefully and can be restarted by the health monitor on the next cycle, rather than taking down the entire gateway process.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `extensions/discord/src/monitor/provider.lifecycle.ts`\\n\\nFixes #56588\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56664/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663\",\"id\":4161981190,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUwbz\",\"number\":56663,\"title\":\"fix(tts): add verbose logging for TTS provider fallback debugging\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"ericpearson\",\"id\":793594,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MzU5NA==\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/793594?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ericpearson\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ericpearson/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:45:13Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:20:32Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56663\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56663.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen Discord auto TTS is configured with ElevenLabs, it silently falls back to Edge TTS without any error message. This adds verbose logging to help diagnose TTS provider selection and fallback issues.\\n\\nThis is a reworked version of #46042 that addresses all review feedback:\\n\\n- **Fixed dead `else if` condition**: The original PR had `else if (errors.length > 0)` which was always true because `errors.push()` ran before the check. Now uses a clean `if (provider === primaryProvider)` / `else` pattern to distinguish primary vs fallback failure messages.\\n- **Fixed double disk read**: `getTtsProvider()` does a synchronous file read internally. The original PR called it unconditionally in `maybeApplyTtsToPayload` for logging, then it was called again inside `textToSpeech`. Now wrapped in an `isVerbose()` guard so the extra call is skipped when verbose logging is disabled.\\n- **Fixed wrong provider logged**: The original PR logged the provider selection *before* `parseTtsDirectives()` ran, so directive overrides were not reflected. Now the log is emitted *after* directives are parsed, and if there's a provider override directive, it reports that provider instead.\\n\\nWith verbose logging enabled (`-v` flag), users will see:\\n- `TTS: auto mode enabled (always), channel=discord, selected provider=elevenlabs, ...`\\n- `TTS: starting with provider elevenlabs, fallbacks: openai, edge`\\n- `TTS: primary provider elevenlabs failed (elevenlabs: no API key); trying fallback providers.`\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] Run with `-v` flag and `messages.tts.provider: elevenlabs` configured — verify correct provider name appears in logs\\n- [ ] Verify primary provider failure shows \\\"primary provider ... failed\\\" message\\n- [ ] Verify fallback provider failure shows \\\"trying next provider\\\" message\\n- [ ] Verify without `-v` flag, no extra disk reads occur (no `getTtsProvider` call in `maybeApplyTtsToPayload`)\\n- [ ] Verify with a TTS directive override, the log reflects the override provider, not the config provider\\n\\nFixes: #46015\\nSupersedes: #46042\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56663/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662\",\"id\":4161972564,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUu9H\",\"number\":56662,\"title\":\"fix: allow microphone access in Permissions-Policy for web UI voice input\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"AlanKharebov\",\"id\":17842209,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQyMjA5\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17842209?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/AlanKharebov\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/AlanKharebov/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10064298757,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDBQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/app:%20web-ui\",\"name\":\"app: web-ui\",\"color\":\"6f42c1\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"App: web-ui\"},{\"id\":10064298857,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDaQ\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/gateway\",\"name\":\"gateway\",\"color\":\"d4c5f9\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Gateway runtime\"},{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:39:58Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:47:29Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56662\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56662.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n- The Control UI includes a voice input (STT) button that uses the Web Speech API\\n- The gateway's `Permissions-Policy` header sets `microphone=()` which blocks all microphone access\\n- This causes Chrome to reject mic permission with \\\"Permissions policy violation: microphone is not allowed in this document\\\" even on HTTPS\\n- Changed to `microphone=(self)` to allow same-origin mic access while still blocking third-party iframes\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [ ] Start gateway with TLS enabled (`gateway.tls.enabled: true`)\\n- [ ] Open Control UI in Chrome\\n- [ ] Click the mic button in the chat input\\n- [ ] Verify Chrome prompts for microphone permission\\n- [ ] Verify voice input transcribes speech into the message box\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56662/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661\",\"id\":4161962732,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874EoLs\",\"number\":56661,\"title\":\"Config validator warns 'plugin not found: google' for entry it just auto-enabled\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"StevenVincentOne\",\"id\":184011678,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOCvfLng\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184011678?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/StevenVincentOne\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/StevenVincentOne/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:33:30Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:33:30Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen `google-gemini-cli` OAuth auth is configured, OpenClaw's own startup routine auto-enables the `google` plugin by writing it into `plugins.allow` and `plugins.entries`, then immediately fires a config validator warning saying those entries are stale. The gateway writes the entry, then warns about the entry it just wrote.\\n\\n## Version\\n\\n`2026.3.24`\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n1. Have a `google-gemini-cli` OAuth auth profile configured in `openclaw.json`\\n2. Start or restart the gateway\\n3. Run any CLI command: `openclaw gateway status`, `openclaw doctor`, `openclaw gateway restart`\\n\\n## Observed behavior\\n\\nThe startup log shows the auto-enable:\\n```\\n[gateway] auto-enabled plugins:\\n- google-gemini-cli auth configured, enabled automatically.\\n```\\n\\nThen immediately, every CLI command spams the following warning — **once per plugin being evaluated** (≈82 times with the default stock plugins dir):\\n\\n```\\nConfig warnings:\\\\n- plugins.entries.google: plugin not found: google (stale config entry ignored; remove it from plugins config)\\n- plugins.allow: plugin not found: google (stale config entry ignored; remove it from plugins config)\\n```\\n\\nRunning `openclaw gateway restart` in a terminal without `OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR` set produced **1,762 occurrences** of the google warning in a single invocation.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nTwo issues compound:\\n\\n**1. Contradictory behavior:** The auto-enable feature writes `google` into `plugins.allow` and `plugins.entries`, but the config validator treats those same entries as stale/unknown and tells the user to remove them. OpenClaw is flagging as stale an entry it added itself.\\n\\n**2. Validator fires before stock plugin scan:** The config validator runs before `OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR` is scanned, so it can't resolve `google` as a known stock plugin at validation time. When the validator does eventually find and load the plugin (`openclaw plugins list` shows `google` as `status: loaded` from `stock:google/index.js`), there's no warning — but by then the damage to CLI output is done. The warning fires once per plugin load iteration, multiplying the output.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n- The config validator should not warn about entries that were written by openclaw's own auto-enable routine in the same startup cycle\\n- OR the validator should run after (or have visibility into) stock plugins so it can resolve `google` as valid before firing\\n- Either way, the warning should fire at most once, not once per plugin being evaluated\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nSetting `OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR` to the openclaw `dist/extensions` directory (where the `google` stock plugin lives) reduces the warning to 2 occurrences (one per validation check). This confirms the multiplier is the validator iterating over plugins without being able to resolve stock plugin IDs:\\n\\n```\\nexport OPENCLAW_BUNDLED_PLUGINS_DIR=\\\"$HOME/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions\\\"\\n```\\n\\nNote: this env var also needs to be set for channel plugins (discord/telegram) to correctly resolve their `../../`-relative shared chunk imports when placed outside the `dist/extensions/` tree — so this setting has value beyond just suppressing the warning.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56661/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660\",\"id\":4161961991,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUtO9\",\"number\":56660,\"title\":\"fix(compaction): use model override in overflow and timeout recovery paths\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"yangyitao100\",\"id\":115475729,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBuIFEQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115475729?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/yangyitao100\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/yangyitao100/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10069976942,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/agents\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"color\":\"5319e7\",\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\"},{\"id\":10190106648,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20S\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:33:01Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T00:25:32Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56660\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56660.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nWhen `agents.defaults.compaction.model` is configured to route compaction through a different model, the override is correctly used for normal LCM compaction but **ignored** in the overflow recovery and timeout recovery paths. This causes HTTP 400 failures when the session's default model cannot handle the compaction request.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nIn `src/agents/pi-embedded-runner/run.ts`, both the overflow recovery (~line 788) and timeout recovery (~line 641) code paths build their runtime context using the session's `provider`/`modelId` variables directly, without consulting `compactionModelOverride` from `agents.defaults.compaction.model`.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Added compaction model override resolution in both overflow and timeout recovery paths\\n- Parses `agents.defaults.compaction.model` config (supports both `provider/model` and `model` formats)\\n- Falls back to session default model when no override is configured\\n- Consistent with existing logic in `compact.ts`\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `src/agents/pi-embedded-runner/run.ts` — overflow and timeout recovery model resolution\\n\\nFixes #56649\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":1,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56660/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659\",\"id\":4161961789,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874En89\",\"number\":56659,\"title\":\"requireMention: false and /activation always don't work in Telegram forum topics\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"ariel-gil\",\"id\":105164685,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOBkSvjQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105164685?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ariel-gil\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ariel-gil/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:32:54Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:32:54Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Environment\\n- OpenClaw 2026.3.22 (4dcc39c)\\n- Node 22, Ubuntu 24.04\\n- Telegram bot with `can_read_all_group_messages: true` (BotFather privacy mode disabled)\\n\\n## Config (redacted)\\n```json5\\nchannels: {\\n  telegram: {\\n    enabled: true,\\n    groupPolicy: \\\"open\\\",\\n    groups: {\\n      \\\"*\\\": { requireMention: false }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Behavior\\n- Bot responds to @mentions and `/commands` in a Telegram forum supergroup\\n- Bot does NOT respond to regular (unmentioned) messages in forum topics\\n- `/status` shows `Activation: always` after running `/activation always`\\n- `openclaw channels status` shows `groups:unmentioned` (config is loaded correctly)\\n- Telegram API confirms `can_read_all_group_messages: true`\\n- DMs work perfectly\\n- Bot was removed and re-added to group after privacy mode change\\n\\n## Expected\\nBot should respond to all messages in forum topics when `requireMention: false` and/or `/activation always` is set.\\n\\n## Steps to reproduce\\n1. Create a Telegram forum supergroup\\n2. Add bot (with privacy mode disabled in BotFather)\\n3. Set `groups: { \\\"*\\\": { requireMention: false } }` in config\\n4. Send `/activation always` in the group\\n5. Send a regular message (no @mention) in a topic\\n6. Bot does not respond\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56659/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658\",\"id\":4161948500,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOQb6kR874EktU\",\"number\":56658,\"title\":\"OpenAI Codex OAuth login requests missing scope `model.request`, causing 401 on all model calls\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"fireniko\",\"id\":211585889,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODJyLYQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/211585889?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/fireniko\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/fireniko/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:26:00Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:26:00Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"**OpenClaw version:** 2026.3.24 (cff6dc9)\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOpenAI Codex OAuth login succeeds, but any request to `openai-codex/gpt-5.4` fails with:\\n\\n```\\nHTTP 401: You have insufficient permissions for this operation. Missing scopes: model.request\\n```\\n\\n## What I verified\\n\\n- OpenAI Platform org/project roles are correct\\n- Account is Organization Owner\\n- Project membership is present\\n- OAuth login completes successfully\\n- Tokens are stored and shown as valid in `openclaw models status`\\n- `openclaw models status --probe --probe-provider openai-codex` fails for all OAuth profiles with the same error\\n\\n## Important evidence\\n\\nThe authorization URL generated by OpenClaw is:\\n\\n```\\nhttps://auth.openai.com/oauth/authorize?...&scope=openid profile email offline_access&...\\n```\\n\\nThe callback URL also returns:\\n\\n```\\nscope=openid profile email offline_access\\n```\\n\\nSo `model.request` is **never requested/granted** during OAuth, which appears to be why all model calls fail.\\n\\n## Expected\\n\\nOpenClaw should request the scopes required to call OpenAI Codex models.\\n\\n## Actual\\n\\nOAuth succeeds, but model requests fail with missing scope `model.request`.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56658/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657\",\"id\":4161943758,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUp18\",\"number\":56657,\"title\":\"fix: sanitize scoped package names in clawhub archive path\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mcgheeloans\",\"id\":260988072,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOD45cqA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260988072?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mcgheeloans\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mcgheeloans/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:23:37Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:32:40Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56657\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56657.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFixes #53870\\n\\nScoped npm package names (e.g. `@openclaw/matrix`) contain a `/` character. When `downloadClawHubPackageArchive` builds the temp archive path using:\\n\\n```js\\nconst archivePath = path.join(tmpDir, `${params.name}.zip`);\\n```\\n\\n`path.join` interprets the `/` in the scope as a directory separator, producing a path like `/tmp/openclaw-clawhub-package-XXXX/@openclaw/matrix.zip`. The subdirectory `@openclaw/` does not exist inside the temp dir, so `fs.writeFile` throws `ENOENT` and the install fails entirely.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`params.name` for a scoped package contains a literal `/` (e.g. `@openclaw/matrix`). `path.join` normalizes paths — it does not escape special characters — so the `/` becomes a real directory separator in the resulting path.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nReplace any `/` characters in the package name with `-` before using it as a filename component, as suggested by @mcgheeloans in [the issue comment](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53870#issuecomment-4148435810):\\n\\n```js\\n// Before\\nconst archivePath = path.join(tmpDir, `${params.name}.zip`);\\n\\n// After\\nconst archivePath = path.join(tmpDir, `${params.name.replace(/\\\\//g, \\\"-\\\")}.zip`);\\n```\\n\\nThis produces a flat filename like `@openclaw-matrix.zip` that sits directly inside the already-created `tmpDir`, resolving the `ENOENT`.\\n\\n**File changed:** `src/infra/clawhub.ts` — one line in `downloadClawHubPackageArchive`.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] Install a non-scoped package (e.g. `clawhub:my-plugin`) — should continue to work as before\\n- [ ] Install a scoped package (e.g. `clawhub:@openclaw/matrix`) — should no longer throw `ENOENT`\\n- [ ] Verify the temp archive file is created and cleaned up correctly after install\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56657/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656\",\"id\":4161943745,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOQb6kR87OUp1x\",\"number\":56656,\"title\":\"fix(plugins): rescue bundled channels from allowlist exclusion\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"hclsys\",\"id\":7755017,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTUwMTc=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7755017?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hclsys\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hclsys/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":10190106613,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/size:%20XS\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"color\":\"b76e79\",\"default\":false,\"description\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:23:36Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-28T23:26:00Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56656\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56656.patch\",\"merged_at\":null},\"body\":\"lobster-biscuit\\n\\nCloses #56426\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSetting `plugins.allow: [\\\"duckduckgo\\\", \\\"google\\\"]` silently breaks Telegram (and other configured bundled channels). The channel stops loading with no error.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`src/plugins/config-state.ts:305` — `resolveEffectiveEnableState()` rescues bundled plugins disabled by the default-off heuristic (`reason === \\\"bundled (disabled by default)\\\"`), but does NOT rescue those disabled by the allowlist (`reason === \\\"not in allowlist\\\"`).\\n\\nWhen `plugins.allow` is set, bundled channels not listed get `reason: \\\"not in allowlist\\\"`. The rescue at line 303-308 only checks for `\\\"bundled (disabled by default)\\\"`, so it misses them.\\n\\n`isBundledChannelEnabledByChannelConfig()` (line 276) already correctly checks whether the channel is explicitly configured (e.g. `channels.telegram.enabled: true`). This should trump the allowlist for bundled channels.\\n\\n## User impact\\n\\nAny user who sets `plugins.allow` to restrict third-party plugins will silently lose all bundled channel plugins (Telegram, Discord, Slack, etc.) that aren't listed. No error message — channels just stop working.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nExtend the rescue condition to also match `reason === \\\"not in allowlist\\\"` for bundled-origin plugins. Added `params.origin === \\\"bundled\\\"` guard to prevent rescuing external plugins the user intentionally excluded.\\n\\n1 file, +3/-1.\\n\\n## How to verify\\n\\n1. Set `plugins.allow: [\\\"duckduckgo\\\"]` + `channels.telegram.enabled: true`\\n2. Before: Telegram silently disabled. After: Telegram loads correctly.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`resolveEffectiveEnableState` is tested in `config-state.test.ts`. The fix adds one additional OR condition to the existing rescue path. Existing tests for the \\\"bundled (disabled by default)\\\" rescue remain valid.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/reactions\",\"total_count\":2,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56656/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null}]","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774745835371}}
{"type":"message","id":"23e47a80","parentId":"27d6920c","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:57:34.165Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"扫描结果很丰富！看到大量新 PR 和 issue。让我重点关注：\n\n1. **#56686** - WhatsApp quoted outbound replies fix - 新 PR，size M，有测试覆盖，可以 review\n2. **#56685** - docs: fix subagent context file list - docs PR，size XS，subagent 相关我们可以 review\n3. **#56684** - Claude-mem integration duplicates session init - 新 issue，memory 相关，multi-agent 有影响\n4. **#56683** - Fix 401/403 auth failures being misclassified as rate limits - PR，size S，fix #47720\n5. **#56682** - webchat session context lost after restart - issue，webchat 相关\n\n\n6. **#56681** - Docker BuildKit regression - regression bug\n7. **#56680** - TTS directive parser treats literal [[tts:...]] examples as active - bug\n8. **#56676** - read tool allowed but not executed, agent fakes output - **严重 bug**，多渠道复现\n9. **#56678** - fix media-understanding for openai-codex/github-copilot - PR size S\n10. **#56677** - fix(Slack) streaming mutual exclusion - PR size\n\n几个问题值得优先关注：#56676 中 read 工具被配置允许却没真正执行是个严重的多渠道 bug，#56686 的 WhatsApp 引用回复功能需要 review，还有 #56685 关于 subagent context 的文档修复和 #56683 关于 401/403 误分类的 PR。\n\n同时注意到 #56684 的 Claude-mem 会话初始化重复问题，#56682 的 webchat 重启后会话丢失，以及 #56680 的 TTS 指令解析器 bug。我需要检查之前的 issue 和 PR 状态，扫描新增的 PR 后决定支持哪些，重点关注那些修复了已知 bug 且 size 较小的 PR，以及新发现的重要 issue。\n\n对于 size XS/S 的 PR 可以快速支持，size M 的选择性支持。","thinkingSignature":"5aa775ca7645dfac1f2a06b0d600c2121b2f5801cf94e6a294cb918c05163c50"},{"type":"text","text":"好！扫描到大量新 PR 和 issue。让我继续检查我们已有 PR 的状态，然后选择可支持的候选：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5pacbvr4q1mg_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace && gh issue view 54952 --json comments,updatedAt --jq '{comments: [.comments[] | {user: .user.login, body: .body[0:200]}], updatedAt}' 2>/dev/null","timeout":20}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5pacbvr4q1mg_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace && gh pr view 55008 --json comments,reviews,updatedAt --jq '{comments: [.comments[] | {user: .user.login, body: .body[0:100]}], reviews: [.reviews[] | select(.state == \"COMMENT\" or .state == \"APPROVED\") | {user: .user.login, state, body: .body[0:80]}], updatedAt}' 2>/dev/null","timeout":20}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5pacbvr4q1mg_3","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace && gh pr view 55013 --json comments,reviews,updatedAt --jq '{comments: [.comments[] | {user: .user.login, body: .body[0:100]}], reviews: [.reviews[] | select(.state == \"COMMENT\" or .state == \"APPROVED\") | {user: .user.login, state, body: .body[0:80]}], updatedAt}' 2>/dev/null","timeout":20}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":73495,"output":790,"cacheRead":22797,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":97082,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774745835395,"responseId":"0617abebecca7899b48c409c0a0e1bef"}}
