{"type":"message","id":"8bb8c4f6","parentId":"3e537070","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:58:42.736Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"评论成功！继续给 #56666 写评论：","thinkingSignature":"6e326421aac058ea78b9e7fc5d3fade41f88045c6150557c26bc05f80e8ddaa4"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5mxfcflwmz8x_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace && gh pr comment 56666 --body \"## PR Review: pinned channel registry fix\n\n**Approve.** The root cause analysis is correct and the fix is minimal.\n\n**Verification:**\n- \\`getChannelPlugin()\\` already uses \\`requireActivePluginChannelRegistry()\\` (pinned), but \\`createChannelRegistryLoader()\\` was using \\`getActivePluginRegistry()\\` (active, mutable) — this inconsistency caused the mismatch\n- The fix aligns both code paths to use the pinned registry, which is designed to survive capability-provider reloads\n- The repro steps are clear: media message → capability reload → active registry loses channel entries → delivery fails\n\n**One observation:** The regression scenario (WS RPC agent dispatch with \\`deliver: true\\` + media message trigger) is quite specific but plausible in multi-agent setups where different agents share the same channel registry. The bounded 100-entry cache for WAMessages is a sensible boundary.\n\n**LGTM.**\n\n---\n*Reviewed as part of OpenClaw community contribution tracking*\" --repo openclaw/openclaw 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":78196,"output":278,"cacheRead":22797,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":101271,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774745915796,"responseId":"0617ac3bb63bacc8f673918062ffb771"}}
{"type":"message","id":"9e0313fb","parentId":"8bb8c4f6","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:58:43.961Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_5mxfcflwmz8x_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666#issuecomment-4149145266"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1198,"aggregated":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56666#issuecomment-4149145266","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774745923946}}
{"type":"message","id":"43141e7f","parentId":"9e0313fb","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:58:52.135Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"继续给 #56686 写评论：","thinkingSignature":"21c82fb0a42e53bbf90e01a7bf2118f4d9576e16b28023077218e531d430af23"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_fgdm3b56isrq_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace && gh pr comment 56686 --body \"## PR Review: WhatsApp quoted outbound replies\n\n**Approve.** Well-scoped bug fix with solid test coverage.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Root cause is clearly identified: \\`replyToId\\` reached the WhatsApp outbound surface but was dropped before the Baileys send call\n- The fix correctly forwards \\`replyToId\\` through both adapter paths and uses Baileys' native \\`quoted\\` send when the target message is in the recent-message cache\n- The bounded cache (TTL + max entries) is a good safeguard — fallback to plain send when message is no longer cached avoids failures\n- Regression tests were added to cover both forwarding and quoted-send behavior\n\n**Scope boundary is correct:** No new config knobs, no inbound parsing changes, no attempt to reconstruct quotes for older messages. This keeps the fix focused and low-risk.\n\n**One minor note:** The PR mentions \\`openclaw-weixin\\` in the scope, but this PR is specifically about WhatsApp Baileys quoted replies. If WeChat support is also needed, that should be a separate issue/PR.\n\n**LGTM — ready to merge.**\n\n---\n*Reviewed as part of OpenClaw community contribution tracking*\" --repo openclaw/openclaw 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":78510,"output":315,"cacheRead":22797,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":101622,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774745923963,"responseId":"0617ac44828fbd75f0e46e478cd7a0b1"}}
