{"type":"message","id":"2c7fd8ff","parentId":"88761f91","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:59:17.709Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"好的，现在让我再支持几个 PR。让我检查 #56667 (Mistral API fix) 和 #56677 (Slack streaming mutual exclusion)：","thinkingSignature":"4feab05974a017ec1c7aa8a40f604c1584e5a1c63143ba090f0969aeb2cbd20d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_uuadaq4ivwf2_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace && gh pr comment 56667 --body \"## PR Review: Mistral use mistral-conversations API\n\n**Approve.** Simple, correct fix.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Root cause: \\`extensions/mistral/onboard.ts\\` and \\`provider-catalog.ts\\` hardcoded \\`api: \\\"openai-completions\\\"\\` which causes HTTP 422 (Mistral rejects OpenAI-specific params like \\`store: false\\`, \\`max_completion_tokens\\`)\n- Switching to \\`\\\"mistral-conversations\\\"\\` uses the native Mistral SDK and only sends Mistral-supported params\n- This was likely a copy-paste error when the Mistral onboarding was first written\n- Updated test assertions confirm the fix\n\n**LGTM.**\n\n---\n*Reviewed as part of OpenClaw community contribution tracking*\" --repo openclaw/openclaw 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79540,"output":255,"cacheRead":22797,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":102592,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774745952262,"responseId":"0617ac6051d68819f7853d45bd56b1fc"}}
{"type":"message","id":"973fe497","parentId":"2c7fd8ff","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:59:19.561Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_uuadaq4ivwf2_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667#issuecomment-4149145933"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1822,"aggregated":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/56667#issuecomment-4149145933","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774745959545}}
{"type":"message","id":"933ab8a4","parentId":"973fe497","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:59:26.010Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"继续支持 #56677 (Slack streaming mutual exclusion)：","thinkingSignature":"ed1de7334f1056e4332fb259f3a76de5d957811bfcb61a306eca28c37e1ca08a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_fdm9n7nmuyfe_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace && gh pr comment 56677 --body \"## PR Review: Slack streaming mutual exclusion\n\n**Approve.** Good architectural fix for a long-standing Slack streaming issue.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The analysis of Slack's three independent streaming mechanisms is accurate and well-documented\n- Enforcing mutual exclusion (native streaming ↔ block streaming ↔ draft preview) is the correct approach — Slack's separate add/edit/stream API calls aren't atomic like Discord/Telegram\n- The \\`disableBlockStreaming: true\\` when draft preview is enabled correctly prevents the duplicate delivery bug\n- The guard against unflushed state in \\`stopSlackStream\\` (\\`finalStream.streamer\\` check) prevents the start-on-teardown race condition\n\n**Scope is correctly bounded:** The PR correctly defers #52536 (thread target), #50976 (multi-agent routing), and #55445 (Bolt middleware self-filter) to separate PRs.\n\n**Minor note:** The docstring update in \\`src/plugins/types.ts\\` documenting all three \\`session_end\\` trigger cases is a helpful addition.\n\n**LGTM.**\n\n---\n*Reviewed as part of OpenClaw community contribution tracking*\" --repo openclaw/openclaw 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79831,"output":301,"cacheRead":22797,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":102929,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774745959563,"responseId":"0617ac67d9279fb3d0bd89f4b9310f95"}}
