{"type":"message","id":"09beb68c","parentId":"b659255d","timestamp":"2026-03-29T08:00:33.846Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the existing cron jobs in `~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json`. There are already two OpenClaw-related cron jobs:1. `57a448ff-1805-4a54-a6cd-3fcdbb5fb8f3` - Every 30 minutes: OpenClaw contribution project check\n2. `6f8bd6c8-5b5f-4cf7-8e6f-3479fd23fc64` - Every hour: OpenClaw community opportunity scanThese two cron jobs already exist! They were created earlier. \n\nI can see the cron jobs are already configured with the messages and schedules I need. The gateway appears to be running and processing these jobs since they show `lastRunStatus: \"ok\"` with recent timestamps.\n\nThe message for the feedback check job confirms it's monitoring the four specific PRs for new maintainer feedback, and the community scan job is running hourly as intended. I notice the feedback check cron job is set to 30 minutes, so it should trigger soon and execute the scan with recent updates to the project files.","thinkingSignature":"b3030bae01b187db92b717a2f56d25034d69fd618fe55e71c4976033159449b1"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_juydnyiodi3p_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\nfrom datetime import datetime\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor job in data.get('jobs', []):\n    msg_preview = job.get('payload', {}).get('message', '')[:60]\n    schedule = job.get('schedule', {})\n    kind = schedule.get('kind', '?')\n    if kind == 'cron':\n        sched = f'cron: {schedule.get(\\\"expr\\\")} ({schedule.get(\\\"tz\\\",\\\"UTC\\\")})'\n    elif kind == 'every':\n        sched = f'every: {schedule.get(\\\"expr\\\")}'\n    else:\n        sched = json.dumps(schedule)\n    state = job.get('state', {})\n    last = datetime.fromtimestamp(state.get('lastRunAtMs', 0)/1000).strftime('%m-%d %H:%M') if state.get('lastRunAtMs') else 'never'\n    nxt = datetime.fromtimestamp(state.get('nextRunAtMs', 0)/1000).strftime('%m-%d %H:%M') if state.get('nextRunAtMs') else '?'\n    status = state.get('lastRunStatus', '?')\n    print(f'{job[\\\"id\\\"][:20]} | {sched} | last:{last} | next:{nxt} | {status}')\n    print(f'  msg: {msg_preview}')\n\"","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":81917,"output":570,"cacheRead":22713,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":105200,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774771217580,"responseId":"06180f1187a3af41fb623a1fae8b5c55"}}
