{"type":"message","id":"c8aaf0be","parentId":"64c7f699","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:40:27.342Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze:\n\n1. aoao is still running - processing #56853 (still working on it)\n2. xixi scan: last ran at 18:54, next at 21:54 (but we changed it to 1 hour... wait, it says next:21:54? That's odd. The interval was changed to 1 hour so next should be around 19:54 or 20:54. Let me check the cron job state...\n\nActually, the cron job message was updated but the `everyMs` is 3600000 (1 hour) - so next should be ~19:54. \n\nBut the display shows 21:54. This might be because the cron job system recalculates the next run time based on the current time when it loaded the config. Or maybe the edit didn't properly save the everyMs value.\n\nActually wait - I set everyMs to 3600000 (1 hour) and the last run was at 18:54. If it's 1 hour interval, next should be around 19:54. But it shows 21:54. That's 3 hours from now (18:54 + 3 hours = 21:54). This suggests the everyMs didn't actually get saved as 3600000, or something reverted it. Let me verify what was actually saved in the cron jobs file.","thinkingSignature":"5e4637f4a6346b6d4dbf1ca764eef6d377103026c8ce640ff52bdd981befd8b6"},{"type":"text","text":"注意到 xixi 扫描下次是 21:54，但按 1 小时间隔应该是 19:54。确认一下：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_lpoxxsgf2wi7_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('cron/jobs.json') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\nfor job in data['jobs']:\n    if job['id'] == '6f8bd6c8-5b5f-4cf7-8e6f-3479fd23fc64':\n        sched = job.get('schedule',{})\n        print(f'everyMs: {sched.get(\\\"everyMs\\\")} ({sched.get(\\\"everyMs\\\",0)/3600000:.1f}h)')\n        print(f'expr: {sched.get(\\\"expr\\\",\\\"\\\")}')\n\" 2>/dev/null","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":78189,"output":488,"cacheRead":22713,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":101390,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774784412833,"responseId":"0618429d5806279125eb54afa4347eae"}}
